{"id": "reasoning-c8abe54d-3885-504b-8cd5-97e9791ec3f7-0", "sessionId": "d77c8371-229c-7034-6088-eaefcc4b4445", "turnId": "turn-6f19a1036e2fefd5642f253cb635b74b", "createdAt": 1792346778638, "updatedAt": 1792346778638, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "So `resolve_corotational_tangent_mode` with \"work_conjugate\" returns \"work_conjugate\" (explicit request passes through). With \"auto\" returns \"consistent\" if follower else \"rotated\".\n\nCurrent code in nonlinear_static.py:\n```python\ntangent_request = (\n    \"work_conjugate\"\n    if rotating_mpc_present and auto and not follower_active\n    else (\"consistent\" if armijo and corotational and auto else corotational_tangent)\n)\nresolved_corotational_tangent = resolve_corotational_tangent_mode(kinematics, tangent_request, follower_pressure=follower_active)\n```\n\nSo with rotating map + auto + follower: tangent_request = corotational_tangent = \"auto\" → resolve → \"consistent\". So the internal force law becomes consistent (rotated E blocks) instead of work_conjugate. That's R4.\n\nThen the later check: `if follower_active and resolved != \"consistent\": raise NotImplementedError`. This check exists for ordinary corotational (non-MPC) models — follower pressure requires consistent tangent. But for rotating-MPC models, the supervisor adopted: auto selects work_conjugate even with follower loads, retaining external follower tangent terms. So the NotImplementedError check must not fire for the rotating-MPC route with work_conjugate.\n\nHmm wait — but is work_conjugate compatible with follower pressure in terms of the general matrix? The review says: \"choose work_conjugate for rotating-MPC auto even when follower loads are present; retain the external follower tangent, general matrix classification and net-imbalance MPC Hessian.\" So yes.\n\nAlso: \"Explicit legacy rotated/consistent requests on this new route should be refused before constitutive activation with an informative ValueError, rather than silently solving a different internal force law. Legacy models without an active rotating descriptor retain their current explicit-mode semantics.\"\n\nSo the R4 fix:\n```python\nif rotating_mpc_present:\n    req = str(corotational_tangent).strip().lower()\n    if req == \"auto\":\n        tangent_request = \"work_conjugate\"\n    elif req in (\"rotated\", \"consistent\"):\n        raise ValueError(...)  # refuse legacy modes on the rotating-MPC route\n    else:\n        tangent_request = corotational_tangent  # work_conjugate\nelse:\n    ... existing logic ...\n```\n\nAnd the follower NotImplementedError check must exempt the rotating-MPC work_conjugate route. Let me look at that check again:\n\n```python\nif kinematics == \"corotational\":\n    validate_corotational_scope(model)\n    if fracture_config is not None: ...\n    if follower_active and resolved_corotational_tangent != \"consistent\":\n        raise NotImplementedError(\"Follower pressure with corotational kinematics requires corotational_tangent='consistent'.\")\n```\n\nFor rotating-MPC + follower + work_conjugate, resolved == \"work_conjugate\" ≠ \"consistent\" → would raise. Need to allow when rotating_mpc_present and resolved == \"work_conjugate\". But wait — where is this check relative to rotating_mpc_present computation? rotating_mpc_present is computed just above tangent_request. Good.\n\nBut hold on — is the work_conjugate internal force + follower external tangent actually assembled correctly in the force loop? The review says \"Follower external tangent assembly and rotating-map external reduction are otherwise present in the main force/DC loops.\" So yes.\n\nAlso need to check `general_tangent` classification: `general_tangent = follower_active or (corotational and consistent) or ...` — follower_active already makes it general. Fine.\n\nNow, where does armijo fit? armijo_requested requires force control; with rotating map + armijo + auto, current code selects \"consistent\". Under the new rule, rotating_mpc_present + auto → work_conjugate regardless. Hmm, but armijo line search with work_conjugate... The existing armijo check earlier: \"line_search='armijo' with corotational kinematics requires corotational_tangent='auto' or 'consistent'\" — refuses 'rotated'. With rotating map + armijo + auto → work_conjugate now. Is that OK? The armijo restriction was about 'rotated' being not a true Newton direction. work_conjugate is an exact tangent (symmetric), so it should be fine for armijo. But to be careful and minimal: the supervisor decision says auto selects work_conjugate with follower loads on the rotating route. For armijo, the previous behavior selected consistent. Changing that could break the armijo path... but actually with rotating map present, previously auto+armijo → consistent (legacy internal force). Under new rule → work_conjugate. The supervisor says explicit legacy modes are refused; auto must select work_conjugate. I'll apply uniformly: rotating route auto → work_conjugate. That's the adopted contract: \"coupled auto selects work_conjugate with follower loads and explicit legacy modes are refused on this new route\".\n\nNow R1: fail closed before constitutive activation when any other admitted affine equation uses a rotating slave translation as a nonzero master. Where to implement? In `build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map` or in nonlinear_static after building the map. The review says entry: build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map. \"Use the actual normalized constraint equations/coefficients (respecting the compiler's coefficient filtering), not only a check for another rotating descriptor.\"\n\nThe map has T_linear. The rotating slave translation DOFs are entry.slave_u_dofs. A downstream affine equation using slave translation B as master means: in T_linear, row of the downstream slave C has nonzero coefficient at column... hmm, T maps q → u. The dependency structure: T rows for dependent DOFs express u_dof = sum coefficients * q. If C's row in T has support overlapping... no wait.\n\nActually the right check: the resolved constraint graph. The `slave_constraints` dict in build_constraint_transformation has for each slave its resolved masters. But that info isn't returned... `info` contains \"slave_dofs\" and audit. Hmm.\n\nAlternative approach using T_linear directly: For a downstream slave C with equation u_C = c * u_B (+ ...), the T row for C is c * (T row for B) + other terms. But detecting \"uses B as master\" from T alone is ambiguous.\n\nBetter: recompute the constraint equations from the model. There's `_collect_mpc_constraints(model)` in assembly.py. Let me look at how constraints are collected and normalized, and see if I can access the per-slave resolved masters.\n\nActually, the cleanest: in build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map, after building entries, gather rotating slave translation DOFs: `rot_slave_u = set of all entry.slave_u_dofs`. Then re-derive the slave constraint graph via the same normalization the compiler uses. Let me read the beginning of build_constraint_transformation to see the equation normalization and what functions exist.", "summary": []}
{"id": "effect-0366b1be-82e9-5a47-9340-2b9bf26f6d17", "sessionId": "d77c8371-229c-7034-6088-eaefcc4b4445", "turnId": "turn-6f19a1036e2fefd5642f253cb635b74b", "createdAt": 1792346778655, "updatedAt": 1792346778686, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "effect", "title": "file_system.read_file", "detail": {"toolName": "file_system.read_file", "display": {"summary": "Reading C:/Github/ANYsolver/src/anysolver/assembly.py", "content": null, "suffix": "", "verb": "Reading", "message": "C:/Github/ANYsolver/src/anysolver/assembly.py", "settledVerb": "Read", "settledMessage": "C:/Github/ANYsolver/src/anysolver/assembly.py", "statusText": "Reading file"}, "kind": "file_read", "input": {"filePath": "C:/Github/ANYsolver/src/anysolver/assembly.py", "offset": 2, "limit": 150}}, "state": {"status": "completed", "output": {"filePath": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\src\\anysolver\\assembly.py", "content": "Assembly and Solver Module\r\n\r\nThis module provides functions for:\r\n- assembling global stiffness and load vectors,\r\n- applying constraints,\r\n- solving linear systems,\r\n- post-processing reactions, stresses and displacements.\r\n\r\nConstraint handling\r\n-------------------\r\nThe linear solver uses an explicit transformation/reduction of the global\r\nsystem. Fixed boundary conditions and beam-shell MPC/eccentricity constraints\r\nare eliminated before solving:\r\n\r\n    u = T q + u0\r\n    T.T K T q = T.T (F - K u0)\r\n\r\nFor unsupported free-free models, the solver can additionally suppress the six\r\nrigid body modes by solving an augmented nullspace system:\r\n\r\n    [K_red  Q] [q]      [F_red]\r\n    [Q.T    0] [lambda] [0    ]\r\n\r\nwhere Q contains orthonormal reduced rigid-body modes. This gives a unique gauge\r\nfor the displacement field without introducing artificial support stiffness. If\r\nthe load vector has a rigid-body component, the solve still returns the gauged\r\nsolution and reports the imbalance through solver diagnostics.\r\n\"\"\"\r\n\r\nfrom __future__ import annotations\r\n\r\nimport json\r\nimport time\r\nimport warnings\r\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any, Dict, List, Optional, Sequence, Tuple\r\n\r\nimport numpy as np\r\nfrom scipy import sparse\r\nfrom scipy.sparse.linalg import bicgstab, gmres, minres\r\n\r\nfrom .cases import make_result_case\r\nfrom .constraint_audit import constraint_residual_summary, require_valid_constraints\r\nfrom .control import CancellationToken, ProgressCallback, cancellation_safe_point, emit_progress\r\nfrom .element_capabilities import require_model_element_capabilities\r\nfrom .linalg import FactorizationCache, MatrixClass, factorize, factorize_cached\r\nfrom .matrix_assembly import (\r\n    assemble_load_matrix,\r\n    assemble_mass_matrix as _canonical_assemble_mass_matrix,\r\n    assemble_system as _canonical_assemble_system,\r\n)\r\nfrom .nonlinear_state import require_no_native_total_lagrangian_elements\r\nfrom .recovery import ResourceConfig\r\nfrom .recovery_batches import (\r\n    _qualified_recovery_observation_guard,\r\n    _run_with_qualified_recovery_runtime_lease,\r\n)\r\nfrom .threading_policy import resource_threaded, thread_policy_diagnostics\r\n\r\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\r\n    from .analysis_session import AnalysisSession\r\n    from .boundary import LoadCase\r\n    from .fe_core import FEModel, FEMesh\r\n\r\n\r\n_SYMMETRIC_DIAGONAL_EQUILIBRATION_ID = (\r\n    \"SYMMETRIC_DIAGONAL_CONGRUENCE_Q1C_V1\"\r\n)\r\n_SYMMETRIC_DIAGONAL_FLOOR_RATIO = 1.0e-30\r\n_LINEAR_STATIC_BACKWARD_ERROR_LIMIT = 1.0e-10\r\n\r\n\r\ndef assemble_system(\r\n    model: \"FEModel\",\r\n    load_case: Optional[\"LoadCase\"] = None,\r\n    include_mass: bool = False,\r\n) -> Tuple[sparse.csr_matrix, np.ndarray, Dict[str, Any]]:\r\n    \"\"\"Compatibility wrapper around :mod:`anysolver.matrix_assembly`.\"\"\"\r\n    return _canonical_assemble_system(model, load_case, include_mass)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef assemble_mass_matrix(model: \"FEModel\") -> Tuple[sparse.csr_matrix, Dict[str, Any]]:\r\n    \"\"\"Compatibility wrapper around :func:`matrix_assembly.assemble_mass_matrix`.\"\"\"\r\n    return _canonical_assemble_mass_matrix(model)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _constraint_value_map(model: \"FEModel\") -> Dict[int, float]:\r\n    \"\"\"Return fixed prescribed displacement values keyed by global DOF.\"\"\"\r\n    dof_manager = model.mesh.dof_manager\r\n    values: Dict[int, float] = {}\r\n    for bc in model.boundary_conditions:\r\n        for dof, value in bc.get_constrained_dofs(dof_manager):\r\n            if dof in values and not np.isclose(values[dof], value):\r\n                raise ValueError(f\"Conflicting prescribed displacement for DOF {dof}: {values[dof]} vs {value}\")\r\n            values[dof] = float(value)\r\n    return values\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _collect_mpc_constraints(model: \"FEModel\") -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\r\n    \"\"\"Collect model equations and element slave/master constraints.\"\"\"\r\n    constraints: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\r\n    for index, equation in enumerate(getattr(model, \"constraint_equations\", ())):\r\n        raw_terms = getattr(equation, \"terms\", getattr(equation, \"coefficients\", ()))\r\n        term_items = raw_terms.items() if hasattr(raw_terms, \"items\") else raw_terms\r\n        terms: Dict[int, float] = {}\r\n        for dof, coefficient in term_items:\r\n            terms[int(dof)] = terms.get(int(dof), 0.0) + float(coefficient)\r\n        slave = int(getattr(equation, \"dependent_dof\"))\r\n        pivot = float(terms.pop(slave))\r\n        constraints.append(\r\n            {\r\n                \"slave\": slave,\r\n                \"masters\": {\r\n                    int(dof): -float(coefficient) / pivot\r\n                    for dof, coefficient in terms.items()\r\n                    if abs(float(coefficient)) > 0.0\r\n                },\r\n                \"value\": float(getattr(equation, \"rhs\", getattr(equation, \"value\", 0.0))) / pivot,\r\n                \"label\": str(getattr(equation, \"source_id\", \"\") or f\"equation_{index}\"),\r\n                \"kind\": \"equation\",\r\n            }\r\n        )\r\n    for element in model.mesh.elements.values():\r\n        getter = getattr(element, \"get_mpc_constraints\", None)\r\n        if getter is None:\r\n            continue\r\n        element_constraints = getter(model.mesh)\r\n        if element_constraints:\r\n            constraints.extend(element_constraints)\r\n    return constraints\r\n\r\n\r\ndef build_constraint_transformation(\r\n    K: sparse.csr_matrix,\r\n    F: np.ndarray,\r\n    model: \"FEModel\",\r\n) -> Tuple[sparse.csr_matrix, np.ndarray, sparse.csr_matrix, np.ndarray, np.ndarray, Dict[str, Any]]:\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    Build the reduced system using fixed DOFs and linear MPC slave relations.\r\n\r\n    The returned system is K_red q = F_red and the full displacement vector is\r\n    recovered from u = T q + u0.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    constraint_audit = require_valid_constraints(model)\r\n    total_dofs = int(K.shape[0])\r\n    fixed_values: Dict[int, float] = {}\r\n    mpc_constraints: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\r\n    for equation in constraint_audit.equations:\r\n        coefficients = {int(dof): float(value) for dof, value in equation.coefficients}\r\n        dependent = int(equation.dependent_dof)\r\n        pivot = coefficients.pop(dependent)\r\n", "numLines": 150, "startLine": 2, "requestedOffset": 2, "requestedLimit": 150, "totalLines": null, "wasTruncated": true}, "outputText": "", "durationMs": 0.0, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Read", "message": "150 lines from C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\src\\anysolver\\assembly.py", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": "(truncated)"}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
