{"id": "effect-8be85f4e-1a5e-56df-83df-acd2cae3166d", "sessionId": "d77c8371-229c-7034-6088-eaefcc4b4445", "turnId": "turn-6f19a1036e2fefd5642f253cb635b74b", "createdAt": 1792346790809, "updatedAt": 1792346790841, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "effect", "title": "file_system.read_file", "detail": {"toolName": "file_system.read_file", "display": {"summary": "Reading C:/Github/ANYsolver/tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_coupling.py", "content": null, "suffix": "", "verb": "Reading", "message": "C:/Github/ANYsolver/tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_coupling.py", "settledVerb": "Read", "settledMessage": "C:/Github/ANYsolver/tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_coupling.py", "statusText": "Reading file"}, "kind": "file_read", "input": {"filePath": "C:/Github/ANYsolver/tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_coupling.py", "offset": 2, "limit": 200}}, "state": {"status": "completed", "output": {"filePath": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\tests\\test_nonlinear_beam_shell_coupling.py", "content": "\nTests the exact finite-rotation master-slave kinematic elimination:\n    u_b = sum_i w_i u_{s,i} + (R(theta_bar_s) - I) r_0\n    theta_b = theta_bar_s = sum_i w_i theta_{s,i}\nwith state-dependent Jacobian J(q) = du/dq, reduced residual\nr_red(q) = J(q)^T (F_ext - F_int(u(q))), and symmetric geometric MPC tangent\nK_mpc,geom(q, F_int - F_ext), using zero Lagrange multipliers.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pytest\nfrom scipy import sparse\n\nfrom anysolver import (\n    BoundaryCondition,\n    DisplacementControl,\n    FEModel,\n    LoadCase,\n    create_shell_element,\n    solve_static_nonlinear,\n)\nfrom anysolver.assembly import build_constraint_transformation\nfrom anysolver.matrix_assembly import (\n    assemble_load_vector,\n    assemble_stiffness_matrix,\n)\nfrom anysolver.corotational import (\n    build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map,\n    has_nonlinear_rotating_mpc,\n    rotating_mpc_geometric_hessian,\n    rotating_mpc_lever_arm_jacobian,\n    rotation_matrix_from_vector,\n    spatial_moment_from_rotation_covector,\n)\nfrom anysolver.constraint_audit import constraint_residual_summary\nfrom anysolver.elements import BeamElement, CoupledBeamShellElement\nfrom anysolver.mesh_gen import InterpolatedBeamShellMPCElement\nfrom anysolver.nonlinear_restart import model_configuration_fingerprint\nfrom anysolver.nonlinear_static import _assemble_nonlinear_system\n\n\ndef _build_coupled_cantilever(\n    route: str,\n    *,\n    nx: int = 2,\n    ny: int = 1,\n    length: float = 1.0,\n    width: float = 0.2,\n    thickness: float = 0.02,\n    eccentricity: tuple[float, float, float] = (0.0, 0.0, 0.05),\n) -> tuple[FEModel, dict]:\n    \"\"\"Build a cantilever Q4 shell strip with a coupled eccentric beam stiffener.\"\"\"\n    model = FEModel(f\"nonlinear_coupled_{route}\")\n    model.add_material(\"steel\", 2.1e11, 0.3, density=7850.0)\n    r_vec = np.asarray(eccentricity, dtype=float)\n\n    # Create shell grid nodes: x in [0, length], y in [-width/2, width/2]\n    shell_node_grid: dict[tuple[int, int], int] = {}\n    node_id = 1\n    xs = np.linspace(0.0, length, nx + 1)\n    ys = np.linspace(-0.5 * width, 0.5 * width, ny + 1)\n    for ix, x in enumerate(xs):\n        for iy, y in enumerate(ys):\n            model.add_node(node_id, float(x), float(y), 0.0)\n            shell_node_grid[(ix, iy)] = node_id\n            node_id += 1\n\n    elem_id = 1\n    for ix in range(nx):\n        for iy in range(ny):\n            n1 = shell_node_grid[(ix, iy)]\n            n2 = shell_node_grid[(ix + 1, iy)]\n            n3 = shell_node_grid[(ix + 1, iy + 1)]\n            n4 = shell_node_grid[(ix, iy + 1)]\n            model.add_element(\n                elem_id,\n                create_shell_element(elem_id, [n1, n2, n3, n4], \"steel\", thickness=thickness),\n            )\n            elem_id += 1\n\n    beam_nodes: list[int] = []\n    couplings: list[dict] = []\n    beam_base_id = 100\n    mpc_base_id = 200\n\n    if route == \"eccentric\":\n        # Attach beam along y = -width/2 (iy = 0) one-to-one with shell nodes\n        for ix, x in enumerate(xs):\n            master_id = shell_node_grid[(ix, 0)]\n            master_node = model.mesh.get_node(master_id)\n            b_id = beam_base_id + ix\n            b_xyz = np.array([master_node.x, master_node.y, master_node.z], dtype=float) + r_vec\n            model.add_node(b_id, float(b_xyz[0]), float(b_xyz[1]), float(b_xyz[2]))\n            beam_nodes.append(b_id)\n            mpc_id = mpc_base_id + ix\n            model.add_element(\n                mpc_id,\n                CoupledBeamShellElement(\n                    mpc_id,\n                    beam_node_id=b_id,\n                    shell_node_id=master_id,\n                    material_name=\"steel\",\n                    eccentricity=r_vec,\n                ),\n            )\n            couplings.append(\n                {\n                    \"slave\": b_id,\n                    \"masters\": [master_id],\n                    \"weights\": np.array([1.0], dtype=float),\n                    \"r\": r_vec.copy(),\n                }\n            )\n    elif route == \"interpolated\":\n        # Attach beam along the centerline y = 0 interpolated between iy=0 and iy=ny\n        weights = np.array([0.6, 0.4], dtype=float)\n        for ix, x in enumerate(xs):\n            m1 = shell_node_grid[(ix, 0)]\n            m2 = shell_node_grid[(ix, ny)]\n            n1_obj = model.mesh.get_node(m1)\n            n2_obj = model.mesh.get_node(m2)\n            attach_xyz = weights[0] * np.array([n1_obj.x, n1_obj.y, n1_obj.z]) + weights[1] * np.array(\n                [n2_obj.x, n2_obj.y, n2_obj.z]\n            )\n            b_id = beam_base_id + ix\n            b_xyz = attach_xyz + r_vec\n            model.add_node(b_id, float(b_xyz[0]), float(b_xyz[1]), float(b_xyz[2]))\n            beam_nodes.append(b_id)\n            mpc_id = mpc_base_id + ix\n            model.add_element(\n                mpc_id,\n                InterpolatedBeamShellMPCElement(\n                    mpc_id,\n                    b_id,\n                    [m1, m2],\n                    weights,\n                    eccentricity=r_vec,\n                ),\n            )\n            couplings.append(\n                {\n                    \"slave\": b_id,\n                    \"masters\": [m1, m2],\n                    \"weights\": weights.copy(),\n                    \"r\": r_vec.copy(),\n                }\n            )\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Unknown route {route!r}\")\n\n    cross_section = {\n        \"area\": 0.01 * 0.04,\n        \"Iy\": 0.01 * (0.04**3) / 12.0,\n        \"Iz\": 0.04 * (0.01**3) / 12.0,\n        \"J\": 1.0e-8,\n    }\n    for ix in range(nx):\n        b_elem_id = 300 + ix\n        model.add_element(\n            b_elem_id,\n            BeamElement(\n                b_elem_id,\n                [beam_nodes[ix], beam_nodes[ix + 1]],\n                material_name=\"steel\",\n                cross_section=cross_section,\n            ),\n        )\n\n    root_shell_nodes = [shell_node_grid[(0, iy)] for iy in range(ny + 1)]\n    tip_shell_nodes = [shell_node_grid[(nx, iy)] for iy in range(ny + 1)]\n    model.add_boundary_condition(\n        BoundaryCondition(\n            \"root\",\n            root_shell_nodes,\n            {name: 0.0 for name in (\"ux\", \"uy\", \"uz\", \"rx\", \"ry\", \"rz\")},\n        )\n    )\n    model.apply_boundary_conditions()\n    meta = {\n        \"route\": route,\n        \"beam_nodes\": beam_nodes,\n        \"root_shell_nodes\": root_shell_nodes,\n        \"tip_shell_nodes\": tip_shell_nodes,\n        \"couplings\": couplings,\n        \"eccentricity\": r_vec,\n    }\n    return model, meta\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"route\", (\"eccentric\", \"interpolated\"))\ndef test_mpc_descriptor_preserves_model_fingerprint(route: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Calling get_nonlinear_mpc_descriptor must never mutate element.__dict__ or model fingerprint.\"\"\"\n    model, _meta = _build_coupled_cantilever(route)\n    K0, _ = assemble_stiffness_matrix(model)\n    zero = np.zeros(K0.shape[0], dtype=float)\n    _, _, T, _, _, _ = build_constraint_transformation(K0, zero, model)\n\n    fp_before = model_configuration_fingerprint(model)\n", "numLines": 200, "startLine": 2, "requestedOffset": 2, "requestedLimit": 200, "totalLines": null, "wasTruncated": true}, "outputText": "", "durationMs": 0.0, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Read", "message": "200 lines from C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\tests\\test_nonlinear_beam_shell_coupling.py", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": "(truncated)"}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
{"id": "reasoning-575ce20a-1658-5ee8-99ee-191a6aaf0c53-0", "sessionId": "d77c8371-229c-7034-6088-eaefcc4b4445", "turnId": "turn-6f19a1036e2fefd5642f253cb635b74b", "createdAt": 1792346792275, "updatedAt": 1792346792275, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "Good, I understand the test style. Now let me check the remaining pieces I need:\n\n1. The convergence_study.py diagnostic (for deliverable 4 mesh study).\n2. ep_isolation.py (for geometry).\n3. The selection.json for final regression.\n4. scripts/run_portable_ci.py usage.\n\nLet me read convergence_study.py and ep_isolation.py.", "summary": []}
{"id": "effect-34100917-0918-5c43-9dd7-89d9b8aeb305", "sessionId": "d77c8371-229c-7034-6088-eaefcc4b4445", "turnId": "turn-6f19a1036e2fefd5642f253cb635b74b", "createdAt": 1792346792295, "updatedAt": 1792346792329, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "effect", "title": "file_system.read_file", "detail": {"toolName": "file_system.read_file", "display": {"summary": "Reading C:/Github/ANYsolver/.development/nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017/diagnostics/convergence_study.py", "content": null, "suffix": "", "verb": "Reading", "message": "C:/Github/ANYsolver/.development/nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017/diagnostics/convergence_study.py", "settledVerb": "Read", "settledMessage": "C:/Github/ANYsolver/.development/nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017/diagnostics/convergence_study.py", "statusText": "Reading file"}, "kind": "file_read", "input": {"filePath": "C:/Github/ANYsolver/.development/nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017/diagnostics/convergence_study.py", "offset": null, "limit": 2000}}, "state": {"status": "completed", "output": {"filePath": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\diagnostics\\convergence_study.py", "content": "\"\"\"Slice 3 convergence study (reproduces the numbers in HANDOVER.md section 4).\n\nCantilever Q4 shell strip L=1.0, W=0.24, t=0.012, root clamped, centre-line\nbeam stiffener (10 x 40 mm rectangle) at eccentricity +0.04 z, coupled by\nCoupledBeamShellElement (beam node on a shell node) or\nInterpolatedBeamShellMPCElement (bilinear weights) otherwise.\n\nUsage (from C:/Github/ANYsolver):\n  python <this file> linear       # linear static: R1..R5, M1..M5, P1..P3\n  python <this file> nl_small     # corotational 12 kN (~2.5 deg): R1..R3\n  python <this file> nl_finite    # corotational 140 kN (~28 deg): M1..M3, P1..P3\n\"\"\"\nimport sys\nimport time\n\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse.linalg import spsolve\n\nfrom anysolver import BoundaryCondition, FEModel, LoadCase, create_shell_element, solve_static_nonlinear\nfrom anysolver.assembly import build_constraint_transformation\nfrom anysolver.elements import BeamElement, CoupledBeamShellElement\nfrom anysolver.matrix_assembly import assemble_load_vector, assemble_stiffness_matrix\nfrom anysolver.mesh_gen import InterpolatedBeamShellMPCElement\n\nCS = {\"area\": 0.01 * 0.04, \"Iy\": 0.01 * 0.04**3 / 12.0, \"Iz\": 0.04 * 0.01**3 / 12.0, \"J\": 1.0e-8}\n\nMESHES = {\n    # half-density beam (n_beam = nx/2): beam nodes coincide with every 2nd shell row\n    \"R1\": (4, 1, 2), \"R2\": (8, 2, 4), \"R3\": (16, 4, 8), \"R4\": (32, 8, 16), \"R5\": (64, 16, 32),\n    # equal density (n_beam = nx)\n    \"M1\": (4, 1, 4), \"M2\": (8, 2, 8), \"M3\": (16, 4, 16), \"M4\": (32, 8, 32), \"M5\": (64, 16, 64),\n    # non-matching (n_beam = 1.5 nx): genuinely interpolated couplings\n    \"P1\": (6, 2, 9), \"P2\": (10, 3, 15), \"P3\": (16, 4, 24),\n}\n\n\ndef build(nx, ny, n_beam, total_fz):\n    L, W, t = 1.0, 0.24, 0.012\n    r = np.array([0.0, 0.0, 0.04])\n    m = FEModel(f\"stiffened_{nx}x{ny}_b{n_beam}\")\n    m.add_material(\"steel\", 2.1e11, 0.3, density=7850.0)\n    grid, nid = {}, 1\n    for ix, x in enumerate(np.linspace(0.0, L, nx + 1)):\n        for iy, y in enumerate(np.linspace(-W / 2, W / 2, ny + 1)):\n            m.add_node(nid, float(x), float(y), 0.0)\n            grid[(ix, iy)] = nid\n            nid += 1\n    eid = 1\n    for ix in range(nx):\n        for iy in range(ny):\n            m.add_element(eid, create_shell_element(\n                eid, [grid[(ix, iy)], grid[(ix + 1, iy)], grid[(ix + 1, iy + 1)], grid[(ix, iy + 1)]],\n                \"steel\", thickness=t))\n            eid += 1\n    beam_nodes = []\n    for ib, xb in enumerate(np.linspace(0.0, L, n_beam + 1)):\n        b = 10000 + ib\n        m.add_node(b, float(xb), 0.0, float(r[2]))\n        beam_nodes.append(b)\n        sx = xb / (L / nx)\n        ix = min(int(np.floor(sx)), nx - 1)\n        xix = sx - ix\n        sy = 0.5 * ny\n        iy = min(int(np.floor(sy)), ny - 1)\n        xiy = sy - iy\n        cand = [(grid[(ix, iy)], (1 - xix) * (1 - xiy)), (grid[(ix + 1, iy)], xix * (1 - xiy)),\n                (grid[(ix + 1, iy + 1)], xix * xiy), (grid[(ix, iy + 1)], (1 - xix) * xiy)]\n        masters = [n for n, w in cand if w > 1e-12]\n        weights = np.array([w for n, w in cand if w > 1e-12])\n        mid = 20000 + ib\n        if len(masters) == 1:\n            m.add_element(mid, CoupledBeamShellElement(mid, b, masters[0], \"steel\", eccentricity=r))\n        else:\n            m.add_element(mid, InterpolatedBeamShellMPCElement(mid, b, masters, weights, eccentricity=r))\n    for ib in range(n_beam):\n        m.add_element(30000 + ib, BeamElement(30000 + ib, [beam_nodes[ib], beam_nodes[ib + 1]], \"steel\", dict(CS)))\n    m.add_boundary_condition(BoundaryCondition(\n        \"root\", [grid[(0, iy)] for iy in range(ny + 1)], {k: 0.0 for k in (\"ux\", \"uy\", \"uz\", \"rx\", \"ry\", \"rz\")}))\n    m.apply_boundary_conditions()\n    lc = LoadCase(\"tip\")\n    for iy in range(ny + 1):\n        w = 0.5 if iy in (0, ny) else 1.0\n        lc.add_nodal_load(grid[(nx, iy)], [0.0, 0.0, total_fz * w / ny, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0])\n    m.add_load_case(lc)\n    return m, lc, beam_nodes[-1]\n\n\ndef tip(m, u, node):\n    d = m.mesh.dof_manager.get_node_dofs(node)\n    return float(u[d[0]]), float(u[d[2]]), float(np.rad2deg(abs(u[d[4]])))\n\n\ndef linear(names):\n    for name in names:\n        m, lc, node = build(*MESHES[name], total_fz=-12000.0)\n        K, _ = assemble_stiffness_matrix(m)\n        F, _ = assemble_load_vector(m, lc)\n        Kr, Fr, T, u0, _, _ = build_constraint_transformation(K, F, m)\n        u = np.asarray(T @ spsolve(Kr.tocsc(), Fr) + u0).reshape(-1)\n        ux, uz, ry = tip(m, u, node)\n        print(f\"{name}: uz={uz:.6f} ry_deg={ry:.6f}\", flush=True)\n\n\ndef nonlinear(names, total_fz):\n    for name in names:\n        t0 = time.perf_counter()\n        m, lc, node = build(*MESHES[name], total_fz=total_fz)\n        res = solve_static_nonlinear(m, lc, kinematics=\"corotational\", num_steps=4, max_iterations=25)\n        ux, uz, ry = tip(m, res.displacements, node)\n        print(f\"{name}: conv={res.converged} uz={uz:.6f} ux={ux:.6f} ry_deg={ry:.4f} \"\n              f\"dt={time.perf_counter() - t0:.2f}s\", flush=True)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    mode = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else \"linear\"\n    if mode == \"linear\":\n        linear([\"R1\", \"R2\", \"R3\", \"R4\", \"R5\", \"M1\", \"M2\", \"M3\", \"M4\", \"M5\", \"P1\", \"P2\", \"P3\"])\n    elif mode == \"nl_small\":\n        nonlinear([\"R1\", \"R2\", \"R3\"], -12000.0)\n    elif mode == \"nl_finite\":\n        nonlinear([\"M1\", \"M2\", \"M3\", \"P1\", \"P2\", \"P3\"], -140000.0)\n    else:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"unknown mode {mode!r}\")\n", "numLines": 123, "startLine": 1, "requestedOffset": null, "requestedLimit": 2000, "totalLines": null, "wasTruncated": false}, "outputText": "", "durationMs": 0.0, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Read", "message": "123 lines from C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\diagnostics\\convergence_study.py", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": ""}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
{"id": "effect-b4387e8b-20cb-58b0-b6cc-b6804ea7e789", "sessionId": "d77c8371-229c-7034-6088-eaefcc4b4445", "turnId": "turn-6f19a1036e2fefd5642f253cb635b74b", "createdAt": 1792346793683, "updatedAt": 1792346793718, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "effect", "title": "file_system.read_file", "detail": {"toolName": "file_system.read_file", "display": {"summary": "Reading C:/Github/ANYsolver/.development/nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017/diagnostics/ep_isolation.py", "content": null, "suffix": "", "verb": "Reading", "message": "C:/Github/ANYsolver/.development/nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017/diagnostics/ep_isolation.py", "settledVerb": "Read", "settledMessage": "C:/Github/ANYsolver/.development/nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017/diagnostics/ep_isolation.py", "statusText": "Reading file"}, "kind": "file_read", "input": {"filePath": "C:/Github/ANYsolver/.development/nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017/diagnostics/ep_isolation.py", "offset": null, "limit": 2000}}, "state": {"status": "completed", "output": {"filePath": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\diagnostics\\ep_isolation.py", "content": "\"\"\"Isolate the 'plastic stiffer than elastic' anomaly.\n\nMatrix: {shell_only, coupled} x {corotational, von_karman} x {elastic(yield x1e4), plastic}\nPlus beam-only fiber cantilever (no shell) to isolate the fiber section.\n\"\"\"\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nfrom anymaterial import DNVC208MaterialCurve\nfrom anysolver import BoundaryCondition, FEModel, LoadCase, create_shell_element, solve_static_nonlinear\nfrom anysolver.elements import BeamElement, CoupledBeamShellElement\n\nL, W, t = 1.0, 0.24, 0.012\nNX, NY = 2, 1\nR = np.array([0.0, 0.0, 0.04])\nCS = {\"area\": 4e-4, \"Iy\": 0.01 * 0.04**3 / 12, \"Iz\": 0.04 * 0.01**3 / 12,\n      \"J\": 1e-8, \"b\": 0.01, \"h\": 0.04, \"fiber_plasticity\": True}\n\n\ndef material(model, scale):\n    from anysolver.material_curves import DNVC208MaterialCurve as C, dnv_c208_steel_curve\n    base = dnv_c208_steel_curve(\"S355\", 0.012).as_dict()\n    hc = C(base[\"sigma_prop\"] * scale, base[\"sigma_yield\"] * scale, base[\"sigma_yield_2\"] * scale,\n           base[\"eps_p_y1\"], base[\"eps_p_y2\"], base[\"K\"] * scale, base[\"n\"])\n    model.add_material(\"steel\", 2.1e11, 0.3, density=7850.0,\n                       yield_stress=base[\"sigma_yield\"] * scale, hardening_curve=hc)\n\n\ndef shell_model(scale, coupled, fz):\n    m = FEModel(\"iso\")\n    material(m, scale)\n    grid = {}\n    nid = 1\n    for ix, x in enumerate(np.linspace(0, L, NX + 1)):\n        for iy, y in enumerate(np.linspace(-W / 2, W / 2, NY + 1)):\n            m.add_node(nid, float(x), float(y), 0.0)\n            grid[(ix, iy)] = nid\n            nid += 1\n    eid = 1\n    for ix in range(NX):\n        for iy in range(NY):\n            m.add_element(eid, create_shell_element(\n                eid, [grid[(ix, iy)], grid[(ix + 1, iy)], grid[(ix + 1, iy + 1)], grid[(ix, iy + 1)]],\n                \"steel\", thickness=t))\n            eid += 1\n    probe = grid[(NX, 0)]\n    if coupled:\n        bn = []\n        for ix in range(NX + 1):\n            b = 100 + ix\n            mid = grid[(ix, 0)]\n            mn = m.mesh.get_node(mid)\n            m.add_node(b, mn.x, mn.y, mn.z + R[2])\n            bn.append(b)\n            m.add_element(200 + ix, CoupledBeamShellElement(200 + ix, b, mid, \"steel\", eccentricity=R))\n        for ix in range(NX):\n            m.add_element(300 + ix, BeamElement(300 + ix, [bn[ix], bn[ix + 1]], \"steel\", dict(CS)))\n    m.add_boundary_condition(BoundaryCondition(\n        \"root\", [grid[(0, iy)] for iy in range(NY + 1)],\n        {k: 0.0 for k in (\"ux\", \"uy\", \"uz\", \"rx\", \"ry\", \"rz\")}))\n    m.apply_boundary_conditions()\n    lc = LoadCase(\"tip\")\n    for iy in range(NY + 1):\n        lc.add_nodal_load(grid[(NX, iy)], [0, 0, fz, 0, 0, 0])\n    m.add_load_case(lc)\n    return m, lc, probe\n\n\ndef beam_model(scale, fz):\n    m = FEModel(\"beam\")\n    material(m, scale)\n    n = 4\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        m.add_node(1 + i, L * i / n, 0.0, 0.0)\n    for i in range(n):\n        m.add_element(10 + i, BeamElement(10 + i, [1 + i, 2 + i], \"steel\", dict(CS)))\n    m.add_boundary_condition(BoundaryCondition(\n        \"root\", [1], {k: 0.0 for k in (\"ux\", \"uy\", \"uz\", \"rx\", \"ry\", \"rz\")}))\n    m.apply_boundary_conditions()\n    lc = LoadCase(\"tip\")\n    lc.add_nodal_load(n + 1, [0, 0, fz, 0, 0, 0])\n    m.add_load_case(lc)\n    return m, lc, n + 1\n\n\ndef run(builder, kin, steps=4):\n    m, lc, probe = builder()\n    try:\n        res = solve_static_nonlinear(m, lc, kinematics=kin, num_steps=steps, max_iterations=30)\n    except Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001\n        return f\"ERROR {type(exc).__name__}: {str(exc)[:90]}\"\n    d = m.mesh.dof_manager.get_node_dofs(probe)\n    amax = max((float(np.max(np.abs(s.get(\"alpha\", 0.0)))) for s in res.element_states.values()\n                if isinstance(s, dict)), default=0.0)\n    return f\"conv={res.converged} uz={res.displacements[d[2]]:+.5f} alpha_max={amax:.2e}\"\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    which = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else \"all\"\n    cases = []\n    if which in (\"all\", \"beam\"):\n        for kin in (\"von_karman\", \"corotational\"):\n            for lab, s in ((\"elastic\", 1e4), (\"plastic\", 1.0)):\n                cases.append((f\"beam-only  {kin:12s} {lab}\", lambda s=s: beam_model(s, -2500.0), kin))\n    if which in (\"all\", \"shell\"):\n        for kin in (\"von_karman\", \"corotational\"):\n            for lab, s in ((\"elastic\", 1e4), (\"plastic\", 1.0)):\n                cases.append((f\"shell-only {kin:12s} {lab}\", lambda s=s: shell_model(s, False, -6000.0), kin))\n    if which in (\"all\", \"coupled\"):\n        for kin in (\"von_karman\", \"corotational\"):\n            for lab, s in ((\"elastic\", 1e4), (\"plastic\", 1.0)):\n                cases.append((f\"coupled    {kin:12s} {lab}\", lambda s=s: shell_model(s, True, -35000.0), kin))\n    for label, b, kin in cases:\n        print(label, \"->\", run(b, kin), flush=True)\n", "numLines": 113, "startLine": 1, "requestedOffset": null, "requestedLimit": 2000, "totalLines": null, "wasTruncated": false}, "outputText": "", "durationMs": 0.0, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Read", "message": "113 lines from C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\diagnostics\\ep_isolation.py", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": ""}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
{"id": "reasoning-009c8722-a574-5e6e-9237-173f4384bab2-0", "sessionId": "d77c8371-229c-7034-6088-eaefcc4b4445", "turnId": "turn-6f19a1036e2fefd5642f253cb635b74b", "createdAt": 1792346800044, "updatedAt": 1792346800044, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "Now I have a good picture. Let me plan the work concretely. Budget: 2978.65s remaining, 900 reserved → ~2078s for the main work. That's tight for: mesh study (R1-R4 @12k nonlinear + linear, M1-M4/P1-P4 @140k nonlinear + linear), arc reference FE runs (nx8/16/32 × matching/nonmatching × e0/0.002 × 30/60deg = lots of cases), EP DC continuation (direct/interp: full 12 steps, half 6, resume 6, cancel), and final regression (25+ modules, up to 600s).\n\nWait — the arc reference: shell nx8/16/32, ny2, matching (n_beam=nx) and nonmatching (1.5nx), e=0 and 0.002, 30 and 60 deg. That's 3 nx × 2 ratios × 2 e × 2 angles = 24 nonlinear solves. Each on a small model (nx up to 32, ny 2 → ~200 nodes). With JIT off... could be slow. The earlier R1-R3 runs took 2.7-13.1s each with JIT on presumably. With JIT off, could be much slower. Hmm, the harness sets NUMBA_DISABLE_JIT=1. The baseline-slice12 run took 67s for 22 tests. The DC full direct run timed out? No — ep-edge-dc-full-direct EXIT_1 (18s, failed). \n\nTime is a real constraint. Let me think about the total plan and sequencing:\n\nPriority order (per continuation):\n1. Harness fixes + ep_attribution prose (cheap, no numerics).\n2. Source repairs R1, R3, R4, R5 (edits).\n3. EP DC continuation diagnostics + pytest conversion (numerics: direct+interp, each: preyield already done; dc_full 12 steps, half 6, resume 6, uninterrupted 12, cancel). These are small models (2x1 shell + 2-3 beam elements). The earlier ep-edge-preyield took 12.6s for 4 solves. DC solves with 12 steps × 40 iterations on a tiny model... the failed dc-full-direct took 18s and exited 1 (error). Need to see what the error was.\n4. Mesh study: linear (cheap) + nonlinear R1-R4@12k, M1-M4/P1-P4@140k. R4 is 32x8 (bigger). M4 (32,8,32), P4 (32,8,48) at 140k. These are the expensive ones. HANDOVER says R1/R2/R3 took 2.7/5.8/13.1s (with JIT on?). R4 expected 30-40s. M4/P4 similar or more. With JIT off, multiply... risky. Total maybe 300-600s.\n5. Arc reference: 24 solves minimum. Small models though (nx×(ny+1) nodes; nx=32, ny=2 → 99 nodes + beam). But nonlinear to 60deg with dead loads... convergence may be tricky. Each maybe 5-30s with JIT off. Total maybe 300-800s.\n6. Final regression: 25 modules + new ones, up to 600s.\n\nTotal budget available non-reserve: ~2078s. Tight but feasible if runs are efficient. I must be careful: one numerical child at a time, each attempt charged.\n\nStrategy to conserve budget: batch multiple cases per harness attempt (per-case flush within one process). The assignment says \"per-case flush\" — print each case as it completes so a timeout preserves partial output. Good: run mesh study as one attempt with per-case flush; if it times out at 120s... individual diagnostic <= 120s. Hmm, \"Individual diagnostic<=120s\". So each harness attempt capped at 120s (unless final verification 600s). The mesh study M4/P4 at 140k might exceed 120s per case with JIT off. Risky. I can split into multiple attempts, each <=120s.\n\nWait, but actually can I raise the timeout for a diagnostic? The assignment says individual diagnostic<=120s. The harness enforces timeout per attempt. So each attempt <= 120s. Multiple attempts allowed as long as budget remains.\n\nAlso note: the earlier runs used the harness with NUMBA_DISABLE_JIT=1? Let me check the receipt of an earlier run to see the runtime record and how long things took with JIT off. ep-attrib-cr-plastic-6k took 53s for ONE case (6-step force control on 2x1 model). That's with JIT off. Ouch. That suggests solves are slow-ish. The DC full 12-step might take much longer than 120s... The failed attempt ep-edge-dc-full-direct EXIT_1 in 18s — probably an API error, not a timeout.\n\nHmm wait, actually let me check what the receipts say about numba. Let me look at a receipt and the preflight.", "summary": []}
