{"id": "reasoning-ebd93b73-b675-5f7c-866a-b5944288368f-0", "sessionId": "d77c8371-229c-7034-6088-eaefcc4b4445", "turnId": "turn-6f19a1036e2fefd5642f253cb635b74b", "createdAt": 1792346846200, "updatedAt": 1792346846200, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "Good. Now I have enough to write the R2 guard test: build a small coupled corotational model, call solve_static_nonlinear with kinematics=\"corotational\", initial_fields={1: ShellInitialField(membrane_stress=...)} → expect NotImplementedError.\n\nNow, let me start implementing. First the harness fixes (item 1):\n\nHarness findings:\n1. Source identity: harness prepends candidate REPO/src regardless of --cwd. Fix: add explicit source-root argument / exact import routing; record/verify import origin and effective source/test hashes of the selected tree for each attribution run. The harness already has --src-override. Improvements:\n   - When --src-override is given, PYTHONPATH should contain ONLY that src (replace, not prepend candidate). Currently: `env[\"PYTHONPATH\"] = src + os.pathsep + env.get(\"PYTHONPATH\",\"\")` — with src-override it puts override first, but candidate REPO/src could still be in PYTHONPATH from parent env... Actually the parent env PYTHONPATH probably doesn't contain repo src. But the review says \"prepends candidate REPO/src to PYTHONPATH regardless of --cwd\" — the issue: if --cwd is the head_wt worktree, python adds cwd... no, python adds the script's directory. Hmm: when running `python .development/.../ep_edge_coupling.py` with cwd=head_wt, sys.path[0] = the diagnostics dir (script dir), not cwd. anysolver imports come from PYTHONPATH. The clean-HEAD runs used --src-override head_wt/src. The preflight records import origin — good. The fix per findings: \"Add an explicit source-root argument or equivalent exact import routing; record/verify import origin and effective source/test hashes of the selected tree for each attribution run.\"\n   \n   So: (a) when --src-override is set, ensure the candidate src is NOT on the path (replace PYTHONPATH entirely with the override, not append parent PYTHONPATH); (b) record source hashes of the selected tree (hash the selected tree's five source files + tests) in the receipt; (c) verify import origin matches the selected source root — add a post-run check comparing preflight runtime anysolver origin against the expected root, and record mismatch as a flag in the receipt.\n\n2. Exception-proof timing/cleanup: wrap the whole thing so that any exception (preflight TimeoutExpired, Popen failure, parse error) still writes a receipt, updates budget, kills timed-out preflight child, preserves partial stdout/stderr. Restructure: try/except/finally around everything; in finally: kill child if still running, write receipt if not written, update budget if not updated, remove lock.\n\n3. Counts: parse from JUnit or explicit named fields; regex can omit failures. Fix: when running pytest, use `--junitxml` ... but the harness runs arbitrary commands. Better: add named count parsing: support pytest summary line parsing robustly (all variants: \"X failed, Y passed, Z skipped\", \"X passed\", \"X failed\", etc.) — parse the full summary including errors/warnings/xfailed. Simplest robust approach: parse the last pytest summary line with a comprehensive regex capturing all categories. Also verify effective JIT/thread settings from runtime records: preflight should import numba and check `numba.config.DISABLE_JIT` and record it; record threadpoolctl info (already). Add JIT check to preflight: `import numba; info[\"numba_disable_jit\"] = bool(numba.config.DISABLE_JIT)`.\n\n   Hash every new diagnostic/test/oracle input: --hash-input exists; I must remember to pass --hash-input for each new script/test used in runs.\n\nAlso fix: preflight child on timeout — currently `proc.communicate(timeout=...)` raises TimeoutExpired → propagates → finally removes lock but no receipt/budget. Fix with kill and continue.\n\nLet me now also handle: \"recover existing timing evidence and label any uncertainty. No such exception has been observed\" — nothing to recover.\n\nNow ep_attribution.py prose fix: the docstring says \"Decision rules (assignment): lambda < 1 or large independent residual -> solver/reporting bug: repair.\" Correct to adopted decision: lambda<1 + small achieved residual is a valid partial equilibrium (stopped_at_limit with minimum_load_increment_reached), not a solver/reporting bug. Also the introduction \"Competing explanations ... E1 solver/reporting defect: achieved lambda < 1 or a large independent reduced residual\" — the prose should reflect the adopted interpretation.\n\nNow the source repairs. Let me write them.\n\nR1 in corotational.py build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map: after building entries (before returning), check downstream dependencies.\n\n```python\n    if not entries:\n        return None\n    _reject_downstream_rotating_slave_translation_dependencies(model, entries)\n    return NonlinearRotatingMPCMap(T_csr, tuple(entries))\n```\n\nAnd a helper:\n\n```python\ndef _reject_downstream_rotating_slave_translation_dependencies(model, entries):\n    \"\"\"Fail closed when an admitted affine equation consumes a rotating slave translation.\n\n    The rotating map corrects only the descriptor's own slave translations.\n    Any other admitted affine equation that uses one of those translations as\n    a nonzero master would silently keep the linearized lever-arm value in the\n    returned physical displacement, so such compositions are refused instead of\n    being solved on the wrong manifold. Ordinary linear chains and upstream\n    shell row ties remain supported; rotating slave rotations stay linear and\n    are not restricted.\n    \"\"\"\n    rotating_slave_translations = set()\n    for entry in entries:\n        rotating_slave_translations.update(int(d) for d in entry.slave_u_dofs)\n    if not rotating_slave_translations:\n        return\n    from .constraint_audit import require_valid_constraints\n    report = require_valid_constraints(model)\n    for equation in report.equations:\n        if str(equation.kind) == \"support\":\n            continue\n        for dof, coefficient in equation.coefficients:\n            dof_i = int(dof)\n            if dof_i == int(equation.dependent_dof):\n                continue\n            if float(coefficient) == 0.0 or dof_i not in rotating_slave_translations:\n                continue\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"Rotating-MPC route: affine equation '{equation.origin}' uses \"\n                f\"rotating slave translation DOF {dof_i} as a master; downstream \"\n                f\"dependencies on rotating slave translations are not supported.\"\n            )\n```\n\nWait — but the equation that DEFINES the rotating slave translation itself: its dependent_dof IS the rotating slave translation, masters are shell DOFs. Not caught (masters don't include the slave). Good.\n\nBut careful: what about an equation whose dependent is a rotating slave translation and ALSO uses another rotating slave translation as master? E.g., a second rotating coupling using B as translational master: its slave is C's translation, master includes B's translation → caught. Good.\n\nEdge: coefficient filtering — the audit's normalized equations include coefficients as given; zero coefficients filtered? In audit_constraints, normalized_equations include all coefficients from _Equation. _collect_equations probably filters zeros when building masters (line 397: equations.append(_Equation(dependent, masters, value, origin, \"mpc\")) — masters built with filtering? I saw in build_constraint_transformation: `masters = {int(k): float(v) for k, v in constraint.get(\"masters\", {}).items() if abs(float(v)) > 0.0}` — that's the compiler. For the audit, let me check _collect_equations around line 340-399 to see if zero coefficients are filtered.\n\nAlso, does `require_valid_constraints` work when the model has support BCs etc.? Yes, it's the same audit the compiler uses.\n\nOne concern: circular import — corotational.py importing constraint_audit at function call time (deferred import inside function) is safe.\n\nNow R3: nonlinear_static.py n_red==0 branch:\n\n```python\n    if n_red == 0:\n        fully_constrained_displacement = (\n            initial_committed_displacement.copy()\n            if checkpoint_resume\n            else (\n                initial_affine_offset\n                if force_restart\n                else np.asarray(u0, dtype=float).reshape(-1)\n            )\n        )\n```\n\nReplace with:\n\n```python\n    if n_red == 0:\n        # The rotating map corrects only its own slave translations, so the\n        # fully constrained return must use the mapped physical state for\n        # every branch; initial_committed_displacement is already mapped.\n        fully_constrained_displacement = np.asarray(\n            initial_committed_displacement, dtype=float\n        ).reshape(-1).copy()\n```\n\nWait — is initial_committed_displacement mapped in ALL branches? checkpoint_resume force branch: yes (apply_kinematics at 5775). force non-checkpoint: yes (5835-5841). force no initial displacements: yes (5867-5871). non-force (else): yes (5885-5887). So yes, always mapped when map present, and equals the linear vector otherwise. \n\nBut hold on — is `initial_committed_displacement` exactly equal to mapped(initial_affine_offset) in the force_restart branch? initial_affine_offset = force_exact_base_offset; initial_committed_displacement = projected_free + force_exact_base_offset then mapped. With n_red==0, projected_free = T@q where q has size 0 → zeros. So projected_free + offset = offset exactly? _exact_binary64_additive_offset guarantees projected_free + offset == supplied_linear exactly. And supplied_linear = to_linear_displacement(initial_displacements). So initial_committed_displacement = mapped(supplied_linear) = mapped(initial_affine_offset) since offset==supplied_linear when projected_free==0... wait: offset = supplied_linear - projected_free computed exactly such that projected_free + offset == supplied_linear. With projected_free = 0, offset = supplied_linear. Yes.\n\nFor the plain branch: initial_committed_displacement = mapped(T@q + u0) = mapped(u0) since T has 0 columns. Yes.\n\nSo the fix is exact and minimal.\n\nR4: the tangent_request block:\n\n```python\n    rotating_mpc_present = (\n        kinematics == \"corotational\" and has_nonlinear_rotating_mpc(model)\n    )\n    if rotating_mpc_present:\n        requested_tangent = str(corotational_tangent).strip().lower()\n        if requested_tangent == \"auto\":\n            # The exact rotating-map route requires the work-conjugate\n            # internal force; auto selects it with or without follower loads\n            # (the external follower tangent is retained separately).\n            tangent_request = \"work_conjugate\"\n        elif requested_tangent in (\"rotated\", \"consistent\"):\n            raise ValueError(\n                \"corotational_tangent='rotated' and 'consistent' change the \"\n                \"internal force law on the rotating-MPC route; use \"\n                \"corotational_tangent='auto' or 'work_conjugate'.\"\n            )\n        else:\n            tangent_request = corotational_tangent\n    else:\n        tangent_request = (\n            \"consistent\"\n            if armijo_requested\n            and kinematics == \"corotational\"\n            and str(corotational_tangent).lower() == \"auto\"\n            else corotational_tangent\n        )\n```\n\nAnd the follower NotImplementedError check:\n\n```python\n        if follower_active and resolved_corotational_tangent != \"consistent\":\n            raise NotImplementedError(\n                \"Follower pressure with corotational kinematics requires \"\n                \"corotational_tangent='consistent'.\"\n            )\n```\n\nbecomes:\n\n```python\n        if (\n            follower_active\n            and resolved_corotational_tangent != \"consistent\"\n            and not (\n                rotating_mpc_present\n                and resolved_corotational_tangent == \"work_conjugate\"\n            )\n        ):\n            raise NotImplementedError(\n                \"Follower pressure with corotational kinematics requires \"\n                \"corotational_tangent='consistent'.\"\n            )\n```\n\nHmm wait, but there's a subtlety: `resolve_corotational_tangent_mode(kinematics, \"work_conjugate\", follower_pressure=True)` returns \"work_conjugate\" (explicit pass-through). Good.\n\nBut also — does the force-control loop actually handle work_conjugate + follower correctly? The review says follower external tangent assembly and rotating-map external reduction are present in the main force/DC loops. I'll trust the review plus my caller-level test will check the complete derivative via central differences (R4 minimal test). That test: \"check the complete derivative of reduced net internal-minus-external force at a finite state against central differences, including external load derivatives and MPC geometric contribution.\" That's a somewhat involved test. Let me look at the existing test test_reduced_coupled_tangent_matches_central_finite_differences to model it.\n\nAlso \"Add a limiting small-pressure comparison to ensure internal-force dispatch does not jump as pressure tends to zero.\" — compare effective mode with tiny follower pressure vs none: both work_conjugate.\n\nHmm, follower pressure API: how do I add follower pressure to a model? Let me search for follower pressure in tests.\n\nR5: as planned.\n\nNow — the tests. Let me look at the existing test file more to reuse helpers (test_nonlinear_beam_shell_coupling.py lines 348-480 for tangent FD test and 480-618 for the finite rotation solve, 618-686 restart test).", "summary": []}
{"id": "effect-17bd313e-2b3e-5ed7-98eb-659b89def781", "sessionId": "d77c8371-229c-7034-6088-eaefcc4b4445", "turnId": "turn-6f19a1036e2fefd5642f253cb635b74b", "createdAt": 1792346846221, "updatedAt": 1792346846258, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "effect", "title": "file_system.read_file", "detail": {"toolName": "file_system.read_file", "display": {"summary": "Reading C:/Github/ANYsolver/tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_coupling.py", "content": null, "suffix": "", "verb": "Reading", "message": "C:/Github/ANYsolver/tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_coupling.py", "settledVerb": "Read", "settledMessage": "C:/Github/ANYsolver/tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_coupling.py", "statusText": "Reading file"}, "kind": "file_read", "input": {"filePath": "C:/Github/ANYsolver/tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_coupling.py", "offset": 349, "limit": 310}}, "state": {"status": "completed", "output": {"filePath": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\tests\\test_nonlinear_beam_shell_coupling.py", "content": "    \"\"\"Verify A(theta_bar, r_0) and H_b(theta_bar, r_0, f_b) against central finite differences.\"\"\"\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(90210)\n    for theta_scale in (0.0, 1.0e-7, 1.0e-4, 0.25, 0.85):\n        theta_bar = theta_scale * rng.standard_normal(3)\n        r0 = np.array([0.04, -0.025, 0.09], dtype=float)\n        f_b = np.array([120.0, -350.0, 480.0], dtype=float)\n\n        A = rotating_mpc_lever_arm_jacobian(theta_bar, r0)\n        H = rotating_mpc_geometric_hessian(theta_bar, r0, f_b)\n        np.testing.assert_allclose(H, H.T, atol=1.0e-14)\n\n        eps = 1.0e-7\n        A_fd = np.zeros((3, 3), dtype=float)\n        H_fd = np.zeros((3, 3), dtype=float)\n        for j in range(3):\n            e_j = np.zeros(3, dtype=float)\n            e_j[j] = eps\n            tp = theta_bar + e_j\n            tm = theta_bar - e_j\n            up = (rotation_matrix_from_vector(tp) - np.eye(3)) @ r0\n            um = (rotation_matrix_from_vector(tm) - np.eye(3)) @ r0\n            A_fd[:, j] = (up - um) / (2.0 * eps)\n\n            gp = rotating_mpc_lever_arm_jacobian(tp, r0).T @ f_b\n            gm = rotating_mpc_lever_arm_jacobian(tm, r0).T @ f_b\n            H_fd[:, j] = (gp - gm) / (2.0 * eps)\n\n        np.testing.assert_allclose(A, A_fd, rtol=1.0e-8, atol=1.0e-10)\n        np.testing.assert_allclose(H, H_fd, rtol=1.0e-7, atol=1.0e-8)\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"route\", (\"eccentric\", \"interpolated\"))\ndef test_reduced_coupled_tangent_matches_central_finite_differences(route: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Reduced coupled tangent J^T K_T J + K_mpc,geom is symmetric and matches FD to < 1e-6.\"\"\"\n    model, meta = _build_coupled_cantilever(\n        route,\n        nx=2,\n        ny=1,\n        eccentricity=(0.03, -0.015, 0.06),\n    )\n    # Apply nonzero external forces and moments directly to the eccentric beam nodes\n    load = LoadCase(\"eccentric_beam_load\")\n    for idx, b_id in enumerate(meta[\"beam_nodes\"][1:], start=1):\n        load.add_nodal_load(\n            b_id,\n            forces=(150.0 * idx, -220.0 * idx, 400.0 * idx),\n            moments=(12.0 * idx, -18.0 * idx, 9.0 * idx),\n        )\n    F_ext, _ = assemble_load_vector(model, load)\n\n    K0, _ = assemble_stiffness_matrix(model)\n    _, _, T, u0, _, _ = build_constraint_transformation(K0, F_ext, model)\n    mpc_map = build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map(model, T)\n    assert mpc_map is not None\n\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(1337 if route == \"eccentric\" else 7331)\n    n_red = int(T.shape[1])\n    # Finite deformation state with ~25-35 deg rotations and finite translations\n    q = np.zeros(n_red, dtype=float)\n    for col in range(n_red):\n        dof = int(T.indices[T.indptr[col]])\n        if dof % 6 < 3:\n            q[col] = rng.uniform(-0.04, 0.04)\n        else:\n            q[col] = rng.uniform(-0.45, 0.45)\n\n    def full_u(q_vec: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n        return mpc_map.apply_kinematics(np.asarray(T @ q_vec + u0, dtype=float).reshape(-1))\n\n    u = full_u(q)\n    J = mpc_map.jacobian(u).toarray()\n\n    # Check J(q) = du/dq against central finite differences\n    eps_j = 1.0e-7\n    J_fd = np.zeros_like(J)\n    for j in range(n_red):\n        dq = np.zeros(n_red, dtype=float)\n        dq[j] = eps_j\n        J_fd[:, j] = (full_u(q + dq) - full_u(q - dq)) / (2.0 * eps_j)\n    np.testing.assert_allclose(J, J_fd, rtol=1.0e-8, atol=1.0e-10)\n\n    # Evaluate internal force and consistent work-conjugate tangent\n    F_int, K_T, _ = _assemble_nonlinear_system(\n        model,\n        u,\n        {},\n        5,\n        tangent=True,\n        kinematics=\"corotational\",\n        corotational_tangent=\"work_conjugate\",\n    )\n    K_red = mpc_map.reduce_tangent(u, K_T, F_int - F_ext).toarray()\n\n    # Symmetry check\n    sym_err = np.linalg.norm(K_red - K_red.T, ord=\"fro\") / max(\n        np.linalg.norm(K_red, ord=\"fro\"), 1.0\n    )\n    assert sym_err < 1.0e-12\n\n    # Central finite difference of net reduced residual r_net(q) = J(q)^T (F_int(u(q)) - F_ext)\n    def net_reduced_force(q_vec: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n        u_q = full_u(q_vec)\n        f_q, _, _ = _assemble_nonlinear_system(\n            model,\n            u_q,\n            {},\n            5,\n            tangent=False,\n            kinematics=\"corotational\",\n            corotational_tangent=\"work_conjugate\",\n        )\n        return mpc_map.reduce_force(u_q, f_q - F_ext)\n\n    eps = 1.0e-6\n    K_fd = np.zeros_like(K_red)\n    for j in range(n_red):\n        dq = np.zeros(n_red, dtype=float)\n        dq[j] = eps\n        K_fd[:, j] = (net_reduced_force(q + dq) - net_reduced_force(q - dq)) / (2.0 * eps)\n\n    rel_err = np.linalg.norm(K_red - K_fd, ord=\"fro\") / np.linalg.norm(K_fd, ord=\"fro\")\n    assert rel_err < 1.0e-6\n\n    # Confirm K_mpc,geom is non-vacuous: omitting it leaves a large O(||f_b|| ||r_0||) error\n    K_without_geom = (J.T @ K_T.toarray() @ J)\n    err_without_geom = np.linalg.norm(K_without_geom - K_fd, ord=\"fro\")\n    assert err_without_geom > 5.0e2 * np.linalg.norm(K_red - K_fd, ord=\"fro\")\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"route\", (\"eccentric\", \"interpolated\"))\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"control_mode\", (\"force\", \"displacement\"))\ndef test_cantilever_stiffened_shell_finite_rotation_solve_and_wrench_balance(\n    route: str,\n    control_mode: str,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Solve coupled stiffened shell past 30 deg rotation and verify wrench & reaction balance.\"\"\"\n    model, meta = _build_coupled_cantilever(\n        route,\n        nx=4,\n        ny=1,\n        length=1.0,\n        width=0.2,\n        thickness=0.02,\n        eccentricity=(0.0, 0.0, 0.05),\n    )\n    tip_beam_node = meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1]\n    load = LoadCase(\"tip_bending_and_axial\")\n    # Apply transverse + axial force on the eccentric tip beam node so lever-arm\n    # moment (R(theta_s) r_0) x f_b is strongly active at finite rotation (> 30 deg).\n    load.add_nodal_load(\n        tip_beam_node,\n        forces=(-4.0e4, 1.5e4, -3.2e5),\n        moments=(0.0, 2.0e4, 0.0),\n    )\n\n    if control_mode == \"force\":\n        result = solve_static_nonlinear(\n            model,\n            load,\n            num_steps=8,\n            max_iterations=25,\n            tolerance=1.0e-9,\n            kinematics=\"corotational\",\n            corotational_tangent=\"auto\",\n        )\n    else:\n        ctrl = DisplacementControl(\n            node_id=meta[\"tip_shell_nodes\"][0],\n            dof=\"uz\",\n            target_displacement=-0.45,\n        )\n        result = solve_static_nonlinear(\n            model,\n            load,\n            control=\"displacement\",\n            displacement_control=ctrl,\n            num_steps=8,\n            max_iterations=25,\n            tolerance=1.0e-9,\n            kinematics=\"corotational\",\n            corotational_tangent=\"auto\",\n        )\n\n    assert result.converged\n    assert result.status == \"completed\"\n    assert result.info[\"corotational_tangent\"] == \"work_conjugate\"\n    assert result.info[\"constraint_info\"][\"method\"] == \"transformation\"\n    assert result.info[\"constraint_postcheck\"][\"status\"] == \"passed\"\n    assert result.info[\"constraint_postcheck\"][\"max_absolute_residual\"] <= 1.0e-12\n    assert result.info[\"constraint_postcheck\"][\"max_relative_residual\"] <= 1.0e-12\n\n    u = np.asarray(result.displacements, dtype=float)\n    tip_beam_dofs = model.mesh.dof_manager.get_node_dofs(tip_beam_node)\n    tip_rot_norm = float(np.linalg.norm(u[tip_beam_dofs[3:6]]))\n    # Verify finite rotation exceeds 30 degrees (0.5236 rad)\n    assert tip_rot_norm > np.deg2rad(30.0)\n\n    # Verify exact nonlinear rotating-arm kinematic relation at all coupled nodes\n    for coupling in meta[\"couplings\"]:\n        slave_dofs = model.mesh.dof_manager.get_node_dofs(coupling[\"slave\"])\n        u_s_bar = np.zeros(3, dtype=float)\n        theta_s_bar = np.zeros(3, dtype=float)\n        for m_id, w in zip(coupling[\"masters\"], coupling[\"weights\"]):\n            m_dofs = model.mesh.dof_manager.get_node_dofs(m_id)\n            u_s_bar += float(w) * u[m_dofs[:3]]\n            theta_s_bar += float(w) * u[m_dofs[3:6]]\n        expected_u_b = u_s_bar + (rotation_matrix_from_vector(theta_s_bar) - np.eye(3)) @ coupling[\"r\"]\n        np.testing.assert_allclose(u[slave_dofs[:3]], expected_u_b, rtol=1.0e-12, atol=1.0e-14)\n        np.testing.assert_allclose(u[slave_dofs[3:6]], theta_s_bar, rtol=1.0e-12, atol=1.0e-14)\n\n    # Verify spatial wrench transfer identity and global support reaction balance\n    K0, _ = assemble_stiffness_matrix(model)\n    F_prop, _ = assemble_load_vector(model, load)\n    F_ext = float(result.load_factor) * F_prop\n    _, _, T, _, _, _ = build_constraint_transformation(K0, F_prop, model)\n    mpc_map = build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map(model, T)\n    assert mpc_map is not None\n\n    F_int, _, _ = _assemble_nonlinear_system(\n        model,\n        u,\n        result.element_states,\n        5,\n        tangent=False,\n        kinematics=\"corotational\",\n        corotational_tangent=\"work_conjugate\",\n    )\n    out_of_balance = F_int - F_ext\n    reduced_residual = mpc_map.reduce_force(u, out_of_balance)\n    ref_norm = max(float(np.linalg.norm(mpc_map.reduce_force(u, F_ext))), 1.0)\n    assert float(np.linalg.norm(reduced_residual)) <= 1.0e-8 * ref_norm\n\n    # Verify per-slave spatial wrench equivalence:\n    # Since t_i = J_l(theta_i)^{-T} m_i and J_r(theta) J_l(theta)^T = R(theta),\n    # J_l(theta_bar)^{-T} (m_b + A(theta_bar, r_0)^T f_b)\n    #   = t_b - J_l(theta_bar)^{-T} J_r(theta_bar)^T (-hat(r_0)) R(theta_bar)^T f_b\n    #   = t_b + R(theta_bar) hat(r_0) R(theta_bar)^T f_b\n    #   = t_b + (R(theta_bar) r_0) x f_b !\n    for entry in mpc_map.entries:\n        f_b = out_of_balance[list(entry.slave_u_dofs)]\n        m_b = out_of_balance[list(entry.slave_theta_dofs)]\n        theta_bar = entry.master_rotation(u)\n        A = rotating_mpc_lever_arm_jacobian(theta_bar, entry.eccentricity)\n        spatial_torque_from_pullback = spatial_moment_from_rotation_covector(\n            theta_bar, m_b + A.T @ f_b\n        )\n        t_b = spatial_moment_from_rotation_covector(theta_bar, m_b)\n        r_spatial = rotation_matrix_from_vector(theta_bar) @ entry.eccentricity\n        spatial_torque_expected = t_b + np.cross(r_spatial, f_b)\n        np.testing.assert_allclose(\n            spatial_torque_from_pullback,\n            spatial_torque_expected,\n            rtol=1.0e-11,\n            atol=1.0e-11,\n        )\n\n    # Verify global support reaction force equilibrium (including root slave beam transfer)\n    root_reaction = np.asarray(result.steps[-1].support_reactions[\"root\"][:3], dtype=float)\n    applied_total_force = np.array([-4.0e4, 1.5e4, -3.2e5], dtype=float) * float(\n        result.load_factor\n    )\n    np.testing.assert_allclose(\n        root_reaction + applied_total_force,\n        np.zeros(3, dtype=float),\n        atol=1.0e-7 * np.linalg.norm(applied_total_force),\n    )\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"route\", (\"eccentric\", \"interpolated\"))\ndef test_coupled_corotational_split_restart_matches_uninterrupted(route: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Split restart at finite rotation reproduces the uninterrupted solve.\"\"\"\n    model, meta = _build_coupled_cantilever(\n        route,\n        nx=2,\n        ny=1,\n        eccentricity=(0.0, 0.0, 0.05),\n    )\n    half_load = LoadCase(\"half_tip_load\")\n    half_load.add_nodal_load(\n        meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1],\n        forces=(-1.0e4, 0.5e4, -1.25e5),\n    )\n    common = dict(\n        num_steps=2,\n        max_iterations=25,\n        tolerance=1.0e-10,\n        kinematics=\"corotational\",\n        corotational_tangent=\"auto\",\n    )\n\n    half = solve_static_nonlinear(\n        model,\n        half_load,\n        max_load_factor=1.0,\n        **common,\n    )\n    assert half.converged\n    resumed = solve_static_nonlinear(\n        model,\n        half_load,\n        constant_load_case=half_load,\n        max_load_factor=1.0,\n        initial_displacements=half.displacements,\n        initial_element_states=half.element_states,\n        equilibrate_initial_state=False,\n        **common,\n    )\n    assert resumed.converged\n\n    fresh_model, fresh_meta = _build_coupled_cantilever(\n", "numLines": 310, "startLine": 349, "requestedOffset": 349, "requestedLimit": 310, "totalLines": null, "wasTruncated": true}, "outputText": "", "durationMs": 0.0, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Read", "message": "310 lines from C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\tests\\test_nonlinear_beam_shell_coupling.py", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": "(truncated)"}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
