otations)? The review says \"Rotating-slave rotations need not be banned solely because they are downstream: their map remains linear.\" So test: equation ry_C = ry_B → NOT refused. Good discriminating test.\n\nR2 test: corotational + initial_fields → NotImplementedError (guard retained).\n\nNow the EP continuation pytest module. Requirements from continuation item 2:\n- EP isolation geometry & S355 curve; direct (2 beam elements) and interp (3).\n- preyield -2k/node: complete at lambda 1, plastic strain zero, match elastic control. (Already evidenced in ep-edge-preyield; convert to test.)\n- DC uz=-0.20 at original tip probe: num_steps12, max_iterations40, tolerance1e-8; complete, target error<=1e-8 m, positive plastic strain.\n- Split: half 6 steps to -0.10, resume 6 steps to -0.20 with deep-copied initial_displacements/initial_element_states, equilibrate_initial_state=False, emit_restart_checkpoint=False; uninterrupted 12 steps. Compare u/lambda/history within existing restart tolerances.\n- Independent residual at actual result.load_factor <= 1e-7 relative.\n- Constraint postcheck (existing tolerances), full force/wrench reactions (force AND moment balance).\n- Input immutability: deep copies of supplied displacement/state inputs unchanged after successful resume, rejected resume, and cancellation; reuse same inputs for clean resume after.\n- DC cancellation via progress_callback after two accepted increments → SolveCancelled; rejected-step snapshots exclude rejected history.\n- \"Rejected-step snapshots must exclude rejected history\" — need a test where a step is rejected (cutback?) and verify snapshots only contain accepted increments. Hmm, how to force a rejected step in DC? Maybe max_iterations small so a step fails? In DC, if a step fails... does DC have cutbacks? The DC loop: failure_reason breaks... Let me think — in DC, if maximum_iterations_reached, the step fails; does it retry with smaller increment? I saw \"adaptation\" in force control. For DC, not