{"id": "reasoning-625528ba-a56b-5897-aaef-91f5b000a893-0", "sessionId": "d77c8371-229c-7034-6088-eaefcc4b4445", "turnId": "turn-6f19a1036e2fefd5642f253cb635b74b", "createdAt": 1792346898050, "updatedAt": 1792346898050, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "So `_support_reaction_resultants` just sums residual force components (translations 0-2 and rotation covectors 3-5) over the constrained dofs of each named BC. The \"moment\" entries are sums of rotation covectors at the constrained nodes. For the EP model: root nodes have zero rotation (clamped), so covector = spatial moment at those nodes. The moment balance: the sum of reaction covectors at the root should balance the applied load covectors... \n\nThe clean equilibrium statement: the transferred imbalance (after transfer_slave_imbalance_to_masters) at constrained dofs equals reactions. Global force balance: sum of reaction forces + applied external forces = 0 (exact, since the transferred imbalance has zero resultant on free dofs... well, approximately, within residual tolerance).\n\nGlobal moment balance: the reaction moment entries are covectors at nodes with theta=0 → equal spatial moments about each node's... a covector p at a node represents the generalized force conjugate to that node's rotation DOF; the spatial moment it represents is about that node's current position? For a node-based FE discretization, the rotational DOF work-conjugate covector corresponds to the spatial moment at the node (the node's rotation is about its own axis frame). So total spatial moment of reactions about the origin = sum over root nodes (r_i × f_reaction_i + m_covector_i). And this should balance the applied forces' moment about the origin: sum over loaded nodes r_j × F_j (current positions) plus applied node moments (none). \n\nSo the wrench check: \n- reaction_forces = root_reaction[:3]; assert reaction_forces + lambda*sum(F_applied) ≈ 0.\n- moment_about_origin: sum over ro