{"id": "effect-20398199-70ff-5de0-b283-8c32bc1b168d", "sessionId": "d77c8371-229c-7034-6088-eaefcc4b4445", "turnId": "turn-6f19a1036e2fefd5642f253cb635b74b", "createdAt": 1792347019473, "updatedAt": 1792347019520, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "effect", "title": "file_system.search_replace", "detail": {"toolName": "file_system.search_replace", "display": {"summary": "Editing C:/Github/ANYsolver/tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "content": null, "suffix": "", "verb": "Editing", "message": "C:/Github/ANYsolver/tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "settledVerb": "Edited", "settledMessage": "C:/Github/ANYsolver/tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "statusText": "Editing file"}, "kind": "file_edit", "input": {"filePath": "C:/Github/ANYsolver/tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "changes": [{"oldString": "def _r5_model():\n    \"\"\"Master uz fixed, ry free, e=(0,0,e); control the beam slave uz.\"\"\"\n    model, meta = _build_coupled_cantilever(\n        \"eccentric\", nx=2, ny=1, eccentricity=(0.0, 0.0, 0.05)\n    )\n    fixed_uz_nodes = [\n        meta[\"grid\"][(ix, iy)]\n        for ix in range(meta[\"nx\"] + 1)\n        for iy in range(meta[\"ny\"] + 1)\n    ]\n    model.add_boundary_condition(\n        BoundaryCondition(\"fix_uz\", fixed_uz_nodes, {\"uz\": 0.0})\n    )\n    model.apply_boundary_conditions()\n    load = LoadCase(\"slave_uz_load\")\n    load.add_nodal_load(meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1], forces=(0.0, 0.0, -5.0e3))\n    model.add_load_case(load)\n    return model, meta, load\n\n\ndef test_r5_zero_jacobian_control_refused_at_zero_rotation() -> None:\n    model, meta, load = _r5_model()\n    control = DisplacementControl(\n        node_id=meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1], dof=\"uz\", target_displacement=-0.01\n    )\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"zero control Jacobian\"):\n        solve_static_nonlinear(\n            model, load, control=\"displacement\", displacement_control=control,\n            kinematics=\"corotational\", num_steps=2, max_iterations=20,\n            tolerance=1.0e-8,\n        )\n\n\ndef test_r5_finite_state_admits_nonlinear_only_control_and_load() -> None:\n    alpha = 0.4\n    model, meta, load = _r5_model()\n    _, _, T, u0, independent_dofs, _ = _transformation(model, load)\n    mpc_map = build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map(model, T)\n    assert mpc_map is not None\n    dofs = model.mesh.dof_manager.get_node_dofs\n\n    q0 = np.zeros(int(T.shape[1]), dtype=float)\n    independent_index = {int(d): i for i, d in enumerate(independent_dofs)}\n    for (ix, iy), node in meta[\"grid\"].items():\n        if node in meta[\"root_nodes\"]:\n            continue\n        ry = int(dofs(node)[4])\n        if ry in independent_index:\n            q0[independent_index[ry]] = alpha\n    initial_u = mpc_map.apply_kinematics(\n        np.asarray(T @ q0 + u0, dtype=float).reshape(-1)\n    )\n\n    control = DisplacementControl(\n        node_id=meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1], dof=\"uz\", target_displacement=-0.01\n    )\n    result = solve_static_nonlinear(\n        model, load, control=\"displacement\", displacement_control=control,\n        kinematics=\"corotational\", num_steps=2, max_iterations=30,\n        tolerance=1.0e-8, initial_displacements=initial_u,\n        equilibrate_initial_state=False,\n    )\n    assert result.status == \"completed\"\n    uz = float(result.displacements[dofs(meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1])[2]])\n    assert abs(uz - (-0.01)) <= 1.0e-8 * max(abs(-0.01), 1.0e-9)\n    # The proportional load on the nonlinear-only slave direction was reduced\n    # to a nonzero vector at the finite state (admission would have refused it\n    # at the zero-rotation origin state).\n    assert abs(result.load_factor) > 0.0", "newString": "def _r5_model():\n    \"\"\"Root clamp plus fixed master uz; the tip beam slave uz is the control.\n\n    The linear MPC gives u_b,z = u_s,z (the lever arm (theta x r0)_z is zero\n    for r0 = (0, 0, e)), so with the master uz fixed the linear control row\n    vanishes.  The nonlinear position u_b,z = ... + (cos(ry) - 1) e has a\n    nonzero finite-state derivative -e sin(ry), so the same control coordinate\n    is usable at a finite-rotation restart.\n    \"\"\"\n    model, meta = _build_coupled_cantilever(\n        \"eccentric\", nx=2, ny=1, eccentricity=(0.0, 0.0, 0.05)\n    )\n    tip_master = meta[\"grid\"][(meta[\"nx\"], 0)]\n    model.add_boundary_condition(\n        BoundaryCondition(\"fix_master_uz\", [tip_master], {\"uz\": 0.0})\n    )\n    model.apply_boundary_conditions()\n    pre_load = LoadCase(\"bending\")\n    pre_load.add_nodal_load(\n        meta[\"grid\"][(meta[\"nx\"], meta[\"ny\"])], forces=(0.0, 0.0, -6.0e4)\n    )\n    model.add_load_case(pre_load)\n    slave_load = LoadCase(\"slave_uz_load\")\n    slave_load.add_nodal_load(meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1], forces=(0.0, 0.0, -5.0e3))\n    model.add_load_case(slave_load)\n    return model, meta, pre_load, slave_load\n\n\ndef test_r5_zero_jacobian_control_refused_at_zero_rotation() -> None:\n    model, meta, _pre_load, slave_load = _r5_model()\n    control = DisplacementControl(\n        node_id=meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1], dof=\"uz\", target_displacement=-0.01\n    )\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"zero control Jacobian\"):\n        solve_static_nonlinear(\n            model, slave_load, control=\"displacement\",\n            displacement_control=control,\n            kinematics=\"corotational\", num_steps=2, max_iterations=20,\n            tolerance=1.0e-8,\n        )\n\n\ndef test_r5_finite_state_admits_nonlinear_only_control_and_load() -> None:\n    model, meta, pre_load, slave_load = _r5_model()\n    dofs = model.mesh.dof_manager.get_node_dofs\n\n    # Reach a genuine finite-rotation equilibrium with a dead shell load.\n    pre = solve_static_nonlinear(\n        model, pre_load, num_steps=6, max_iterations=25, tolerance=1.0e-9,\n        kinematics=\"corotational\", corotational_tangent=\"auto\",\n    )\n    assert pre.converged\n    tip_master_ry = float(pre.displacements[dofs(meta[\"grid\"][(meta[\"nx\"], 0)])[4]])\n    assert abs(tip_master_ry) > 0.2\n\n    # The same control coordinate and slave-only proportional load that are\n    # refused at the zero-rotation origin are admissible at this finite state.\n    control = DisplacementControl(\n        node_id=meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1], dof=\"uz\", target_displacement=-0.01\n    )\n    result = solve_static_nonlinear(\n        model, slave_load, control=\"displacement\", displacement_control=control,\n        kinematics=\"corotational\", num_steps=2, max_iterations=30,\n        tolerance=1.0e-8, initial_displacements=pre.displacements,\n        initial_element_states=pre.element_states,\n        equilibrate_initial_state=False,\n    )\n    assert result.status == \"completed\"\n    uz = float(result.displacements[dofs(meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1])[2]])\n    assert abs(uz - (-0.01)) <= 1.0e-8 * max(abs(-0.01), 1.0e-9)\n    # The slave-only proportional load reduced to a nonzero vector at the\n    # finite state; at the origin state its reduction is exactly zero.\n    assert abs(result.load_factor) > 0.0", "replaceAll": false}]}}, "state": {"status": "completed", "output": {"file": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\tests\\test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "oldString": null, "newString": null, "occurrences": [{"startLine": 558, "oldText": "def _r5_model():\n    \"\"\"Master uz fixed, ry free, e=(0,0,e); control the beam slave uz.\"\"\"\n    model, meta = _build_coupled_cantilever(\n        \"eccentric\", nx=2, ny=1, eccentricity=(0.0, 0.0, 0.05)\n    )\n    fixed_uz_nodes = [\n        meta[\"grid\"][(ix, iy)]\n        for ix in range(meta[\"nx\"] + 1)\n        for iy in range(meta[\"ny\"] + 1)\n    ]\n    model.add_boundary_condition(\n        BoundaryCondition(\"fix_uz\", fixed_uz_nodes, {\"uz\": 0.0})\n    )\n    model.apply_boundary_conditions()\n    load = LoadCase(\"slave_uz_load\")\n    load.add_nodal_load(meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1], forces=(0.0, 0.0, -5.0e3))\n    model.add_load_case(load)\n    return model, meta, load\n\n\ndef test_r5_zero_jacobian_control_refused_at_zero_rotation() -> None:\n    model, meta, load = _r5_model()\n    control = DisplacementControl(\n        node_id=meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1], dof=\"uz\", target_displacement=-0.01\n    )\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"zero control Jacobian\"):\n        solve_static_nonlinear(\n            model, load, control=\"displacement\", displacement_control=control,\n            kinematics=\"corotational\", num_steps=2, max_iterations=20,\n            tolerance=1.0e-8,\n        )\n\n\ndef test_r5_finite_state_admits_nonlinear_only_control_and_load() -> None:\n    alpha = 0.4\n    model, meta, load = _r5_model()\n    _, _, T, u0, independent_dofs, _ = _transformation(model, load)\n    mpc_map = build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map(model, T)\n    assert mpc_map is not None\n    dofs = model.mesh.dof_manager.get_node_dofs\n\n    q0 = np.zeros(int(T.shape[1]), dtype=float)\n    independent_index = {int(d): i for i, d in enumerate(independent_dofs)}\n    for (ix, iy), node in meta[\"grid\"].items():\n        if node in meta[\"root_nodes\"]:\n            continue\n        ry = int(dofs(node)[4])\n        if ry in independent_index:\n            q0[independent_index[ry]] = alpha\n    initial_u = mpc_map.apply_kinematics(\n        np.asarray(T @ q0 + u0, dtype=float).reshape(-1)\n    )\n\n    control = DisplacementControl(\n        node_id=meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1], dof=\"uz\", target_displacement=-0.01\n    )\n    result = solve_static_nonlinear(\n        model, load, control=\"displacement\", displacement_control=control,\n        kinematics=\"corotational\", num_steps=2, max_iterations=30,\n        tolerance=1.0e-8, initial_displacements=initial_u,\n        equilibrate_initial_state=False,\n    )\n    assert result.status == \"completed\"\n    uz = float(result.displacements[dofs(meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1])[2]])\n    assert abs(uz - (-0.01)) <= 1.0e-8 * max(abs(-0.01), 1.0e-9)\n    # The proportional load on the nonlinear-only slave direction was reduced\n    # to a nonzero vector at the finite state (admission would have refused it\n    # at the zero-rotation origin state).\n    assert abs(result.load_factor) > 0.0", "newText": "def _r5_model():\n    \"\"\"Root clamp plus fixed master uz; the tip beam slave uz is the control.\n\n    The linear MPC gives u_b,z = u_s,z (the lever arm (theta x r0)_z is zero\n    for r0 = (0, 0, e)), so with the master uz fixed the linear control row\n    vanishes.  The nonlinear position u_b,z = ... + (cos(ry) - 1) e has a\n    nonzero finite-state derivative -e sin(ry), so the same control coordinate\n    is usable at a finite-rotation restart.\n    \"\"\"\n    model, meta = _build_coupled_cantilever(\n        \"eccentric\", nx=2, ny=1, eccentricity=(0.0, 0.0, 0.05)\n    )\n    tip_master = meta[\"grid\"][(meta[\"nx\"], 0)]\n    model.add_boundary_condition(\n        BoundaryCondition(\"fix_master_uz\", [tip_master], {\"uz\": 0.0})\n    )\n    model.apply_boundary_conditions()\n    pre_load = LoadCase(\"bending\")\n    pre_load.add_nodal_load(\n        meta[\"grid\"][(meta[\"nx\"], meta[\"ny\"])], forces=(0.0, 0.0, -6.0e4)\n    )\n    model.add_load_case(pre_load)\n    slave_load = LoadCase(\"slave_uz_load\")\n    slave_load.add_nodal_load(meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1], forces=(0.0, 0.0, -5.0e3))\n    model.add_load_case(slave_load)\n    return model, meta, pre_load, slave_load\n\n\ndef test_r5_zero_jacobian_control_refused_at_zero_rotation() -> None:\n    model, meta, _pre_load, slave_load = _r5_model()\n    control = DisplacementControl(\n        node_id=meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1], dof=\"uz\", target_displacement=-0.01\n    )\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"zero control Jacobian\"):\n        solve_static_nonlinear(\n            model, slave_load, control=\"displacement\",\n            displacement_control=control,\n            kinematics=\"corotational\", num_steps=2, max_iterations=20,\n            tolerance=1.0e-8,\n        )\n\n\ndef test_r5_finite_state_admits_nonlinear_only_control_and_load() -> None:\n    model, meta, pre_load, slave_load = _r5_model()\n    dofs = model.mesh.dof_manager.get_node_dofs\n\n    # Reach a genuine finite-rotation equilibrium with a dead shell load.\n    pre = solve_static_nonlinear(\n        model, pre_load, num_steps=6, max_iterations=25, tolerance=1.0e-9,\n        kinematics=\"corotational\", corotational_tangent=\"auto\",\n    )\n    assert pre.converged\n    tip_master_ry = float(pre.displacements[dofs(meta[\"grid\"][(meta[\"nx\"], 0)])[4]])\n    assert abs(tip_master_ry) > 0.2\n\n    # The same control coordinate and slave-only proportional load that are\n    # refused at the zero-rotation origin are admissible at this finite state.\n    control = DisplacementControl(\n        node_id=meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1], dof=\"uz\", target_displacement=-0.01\n    )\n    result = solve_static_nonlinear(\n        model, slave_load, control=\"displacement\", displacement_control=control,\n        kinematics=\"corotational\", num_steps=2, max_iterations=30,\n        tolerance=1.0e-8, initial_displacements=pre.displacements,\n        initial_element_states=pre.element_states,\n        equilibrate_initial_state=False,\n    )\n    assert result.status == \"completed\"\n    uz = float(result.displacements[dofs(meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1])[2]])\n    assert abs(uz - (-0.01)) <= 1.0e-8 * max(abs(-0.01), 1.0e-9)\n    # The slave-only proportional load reduced to a nonzero vector at the\n    # finite state; at the origin state its reduction is exactly zero.\n    assert abs(result.load_factor) > 0.0"}]}, "outputText": "", "durationMs": 0.0, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Edited", "message": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\tests\\test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": ""}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
{"id": "reasoning-75e2bbd4-ff7a-5726-a477-92593a4f93ef-0", "sessionId": "d77c8371-229c-7034-6088-eaefcc4b4445", "turnId": "turn-6f19a1036e2fefd5642f253cb635b74b", "createdAt": 1792347025165, "updatedAt": 1792347025165, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "Wait — there's an issue with the R5 refusal test now: the model has TWO load cases added (pre_load and slave_load). solve_static_nonlinear(model, slave_load, ...) uses only the given load case as proportional. OK.\n\nBut another issue: in the refusal test, the ValueError fires at admission — before that, `build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map` is called (fine), and the DC helper is entered. Good.\n\nHmm, one more concern in the R5 finite test: the pre-solve load is on node (2,1) — with nx=2, ny=1, grid[(2,1)] is the tip corner opposite the beam line. The beam runs along y=-w/2 (iy=0). Load at (2,1) = y=+w/2 tip. Fine, bends the strip.\n\nAlso — the pre-solve: does it reach |ry| > 0.2 at the master (2,0)? Load 6e4 N on a strip with the beam stiffener... The existing finite-rotation test used -3.2e5 z-force on the beam tip node with nx=4 and got >30deg. Here 6e4 on shell tip with nx=2... maybe less rotation. The beam stiffener E*I=1120 N·m², L=1: tip rotation under 6e4 N at tip: M=6e4 N·m, theta ≈ M*L/(2EI)? For a cantilever theta = M L/EI = 6e4/1120 ≈ 53 rad?? That's way beyond — it would rotate hugely or the shell membrane stiffening... hmm, actually the coupled strip: shell membrane action resists. The existing test with 3.2e5 got ~30deg+. With 6e4, rotation maybe ~5-10deg = 0.09-0.17 rad. My assert >0.2 rad might fail. Let me lower the threshold to 0.05 rad (the admission only needs sin(ry)≠0 meaningfully; the discriminating power is fine). Actually the derivative -e*sin(ry) at ry=0.05: 0.05*0.05=2.5e-3 — nonzero. But for a robust nonzero check, 0.05 rad is fine. Let me set the pre-load to 1.2e5 and threshold 0.1 rad. Hmm, but too much load might cause the shell to fold... The existing test used 3.2e5 with 8 steps and converged to >30deg. I'll use 1.0e5 and assert > 0.1.\n\nAlso `assert abs(result.load_factor) > 0.0` — trivially true; better: assert the reduced proportional load at the finite state is nonzero... that's internal. The admission itself proves it (old code would refuse). Keep as is but it's weak; fine.\n\nLet me update the pre-load magnitude and threshold.", "summary": []}
