resume (2 — but cancel's \"reuse same inputs for clean resume\" can reuse the CACHED resume result? No — the cancel test needs its own clean resume after cancellation... it could reuse the split test's resume result IF the inputs are the same deep copies. The cancel test: cancel a resumed run, then \"reusing those same inputs must reproduce the fresh resume\" — the fresh resume is already computed in the split test (cached). So the cancel test only needs the cancelled run itself (~2 accepted steps ≈ 5-8s).\n\nSo per coupling: preyield 2 solves (6s) + full (30s) + half (15s) + resume (15s) + uninterrupted (30s) + cancel (~8s) + rejected (~3s) ≈ 107s; ×2 = 214s. Plus repairs module ~60-90s. Plus slice12 67s. Total new ≈ 350s. Historical ≈ 300-400s. Sum 650-750s > 600s. Over budget.\n\nHmm. What can I do within the contract? \n\nRe-read the continuation: \"Final exact25 historical + two Slice1/2 + newSlice3 modules through portable runner, one verified thread/JIT off/retired0.\" and original: \"Use scripts/run_portable_ci.py --development <targets> --jit off --timeout-seconds 600 --memory-limit-mib 2048.\"\n\nThe timeout-seconds 600 is prescribed. If the suite exceeds it, the gate fails. But maybe my time estimates are pessimistic. The preyield 4 solves took 12.6s (3s each). DC solves: unknown. Let me get data early: run one DC full solve first (one attempt ~60s), then estimate.\n\nAlso — the historical 25 modules: let me look for actual historical timing. The integration-checks dir may have receipts with wall times. Let me check.", "summary": []}
