{"id": "reasoning-72ac9f81-fbbf-5e84-b35c-8892f9f45015-0", "sessionId": "d77c8371-229c-7034-6088-eaefcc4b4445", "turnId": "turn-6f19a1036e2fefd5642f253cb635b74b", "createdAt": 1792347109678, "updatedAt": 1792347109678, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "Important new findings in supervisor_findings.md that I need to reconcile with what was done in the previous session:\n\n1. **R3 selector regression**: \"new R3 selector using initial_committed_displacement in all n_red==0 cases is wrong for fresh force control. That branch deliberately sets initial_committed_displacement=map(T@q) without u0. With no reduced DOFs it is zero even when u0 contains finite prescribed master motion. Preserve original branch selector, mapping raw offsets exactly once: checkpoint_resume -> already mapped initial state; force_restart -> map(initial_affine_offset); fresh -> map(u0).\"\n\nSo my previous R3 edit (using initial_committed_displacement in the n_red==0 branch) is WRONG. I need to fix it: preserve the original branch selector, mapping raw offsets exactly once:\n- checkpoint_resume → already mapped initial state\n- force_restart → map(initial_affine_offset)\n- fresh → map(u0)\n\n2. **Harness recheck**: exception-finally path writes wall_total_final=wall_total but doesn't add elapsed time for interrupted active phase (t0). Need to track active phase start/completion and account elapsed time after cleanup unconditionally.\n\n3. **Test R3 fixture**: current test_r3 fixture first installs zero root supports through its builder, then appends nonzero root rotations, so audit rejects before reaching n_red==0. Replace/remove the old root boundary in this fixture; don't append conflicting supports. Explicitly assert prescribed shell values as well as beam offset.\n\n4. **Follower derivative test**: check the external reduced-force derivative on its own scale: differentiate J(u)^T F_ext(u) and compare to J.T K_ext J + geometric_tangent(u,F_ext), normalizing by that external matrix.\n\nSo there's a \"reviewer addendum\" — I should read supervisor_code_review.md and supervisor_reference_review.md for the addendum details. Let me read those files now.", "summary": []}
