{"id": "reasoning-def93f31-42ca-5e57-bafe-c073183ac91e-0", "sessionId": "d77c8371-229c-7034-6088-eaefcc4b4445", "turnId": "turn-6f19a1036e2fefd5642f253cb635b74b", "createdAt": 1792347146389, "updatedAt": 1792347146389, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "The harness issue: if an exception occurs during the main phase (after `t0 = time.perf_counter()` at line 324 but before `main_wall = time.perf_counter() - t0` at 346), the finally block uses `wall_total` which doesn't include the active main phase elapsed time. Same for preflight phase.\n\nFix: track `active_phase_start` (set at each phase start, cleared at each phase completion), and in the finally block, if `active_phase_start is not None`, add `time.perf_counter() - active_phase_start` to wall_total after cleanup.\n\nImplementation:\n- Before preflight Popen: `phase_start = time.perf_counter()` (replace t0 usage)\n- After preflight completes: `pre_wall = time.perf_counter() - phase_start; wall_total += pre_wall; phase_start = None`\n- Before main Popen: `phase_start = time.perf_counter()`\n- After main completes: `main_wall = time.perf_counter() - phase_start; wall_total += main_wall; phase_start = None`\n- In finally: after cleanup, `if phase_start is not None: wall_total += time.perf_counter() - phase_start; phase_start = None` — do this BEFORE writing the partial receipt.\n\nNote the timeout path: proc.wait raises TimeoutExpired → caught inside → status=TIMEOUT → then main_wall computed normally. That's fine. But an exception in e.g. `kill_tree` or elsewhere between start and completion would skip the accounting. The phase_start tracking handles all.\n\nLet me apply these edits. The harness uses LF endings (v2 rewritten with LF). Let me check.", "summary": []}
