{"id": "effect-281425d7-95e1-567f-b093-841b3fbc4929", "sessionId": "d77c8371-229c-7034-6088-eaefcc4b4445", "turnId": "turn-6f19a1036e2fefd5642f253cb635b74b", "createdAt": 1792347174536, "updatedAt": 1792347174604, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "effect", "title": "file_system.read_file", "detail": {"toolName": "file_system.read_file", "display": {"summary": "Reading C:/Github/ANYsolver/tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "content": null, "suffix": "", "verb": "Reading", "message": "C:/Github/ANYsolver/tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "settledVerb": "Read", "settledMessage": "C:/Github/ANYsolver/tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "statusText": "Reading file"}, "kind": "file_read", "input": {"filePath": "C:/Github/ANYsolver/tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "offset": 501, "limit": 100}}, "state": {"status": "completed", "output": {"filePath": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\tests\\test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "content": "    consistent_result = solve_static_nonlinear(\n        model, follower, num_steps=2, max_iterations=15,\n        kinematics=\"corotational\", corotational_tangent=\"consistent\",\n    )\n    assert consistent_result.info[\"corotational_tangent\"] == \"consistent\"\n    assert consistent_result.info[\"follower_pressure\"] is True\n\n\ndef test_r4_follower_complete_reduced_derivative_matches_finite_differences() -> None:\n    model, meta, load = _coupled_with_follower(200.0)\n    load.add_nodal_load(\n        meta[\"beam_nodes\"][1], moments=(12.0, -18.0, 9.0)\n    )\n    K0, _ = assemble_stiffness_matrix(model)\n    F_ext_ref, _ = assemble_load_vector(model, load)\n    _, _, T, u0, _, _ = build_constraint_transformation(K0, F_ext_ref, model)\n    mpc_map = build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map(model, T)\n    assert mpc_map is not None\n\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(4242)\n    n_red = int(T.shape[1])\n    q = np.zeros(n_red, dtype=float)\n    for col in range(n_red):\n        dof = int(T.indices[T.indptr[col]])\n        if dof % 6 < 3:\n            q[col] = rng.uniform(-0.03, 0.03)\n        else:\n            q[col] = rng.uniform(-0.35, 0.35)\n\n    def full_u(q_vec: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n        return mpc_map.apply_kinematics(\n            np.asarray(T @ q_vec + u0, dtype=float).reshape(-1)\n        )\n\n    def net_reduced_force(q_vec: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n        u_q = full_u(q_vec)\n        f_int, _, _ = _assemble_nonlinear_system(\n            model, u_q, {}, 5, tangent=False, kinematics=\"corotational\",\n            corotational_tangent=\"work_conjugate\",\n        )\n        f_ext, _ = _weighted_external_load_system(\n            model, [(load, 1.0)], u_q, tangent=False\n        )\n        return mpc_map.reduce_force(u_q, f_int - f_ext)\n\n    u = full_u(q)\n    f_int, K_T, _ = _assemble_nonlinear_system(\n        model, u, {}, 5, tangent=True, kinematics=\"corotational\",\n        corotational_tangent=\"work_conjugate\",\n    )\n    f_ext, K_ext = _weighted_external_load_system(\n        model, [(load, 1.0)], u, tangent=True\n    )\n    K_red = mpc_map.reduce_tangent(\n        u, K_T, f_int - f_ext, K_ext if K_ext is not None and K_ext.nnz else None\n    ).toarray()\n\n    eps = 1.0e-6\n    K_fd = np.zeros_like(K_red)\n    for j in range(n_red):\n        dq = np.zeros(n_red, dtype=float)\n        dq[j] = eps\n        K_fd[:, j] = (\n            net_reduced_force(q + dq) - net_reduced_force(q - dq)\n        ) / (2.0 * eps)\n\n    rel_err = np.linalg.norm(K_red - K_fd, ord=\"fro\") / np.linalg.norm(\n        K_fd, ord=\"fro\"\n    )\n    assert rel_err < 1.0e-6\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# R5: displacement-control admission at the actual initial mapped state\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _r5_model():\n    \"\"\"Root clamp plus fixed master uz; the tip beam slave uz is the control.\n\n    The linear MPC gives u_b,z = u_s,z (the lever arm (theta x r0)_z is zero\n    for r0 = (0, 0, e)), so with the master uz fixed the linear control row\n    vanishes.  The nonlinear position u_b,z = ... + (cos(ry) - 1) e has a\n    nonzero finite-state derivative -e sin(ry), so the same control coordinate\n    is usable at a finite-rotation restart.\n    \"\"\"\n    model, meta = _build_coupled_cantilever(\n        \"eccentric\", nx=2, ny=1, eccentricity=(0.0, 0.0, 0.05)\n    )\n    tip_master = meta[\"grid\"][(meta[\"nx\"], 0)]\n    model.add_boundary_condition(\n        BoundaryCondition(\"fix_master_uz\", [tip_master], {\"uz\": 0.0})\n    )\n    model.apply_boundary_conditions()\n    pre_load = LoadCase(\"bending\")\n    pre_load.add_nodal_load(\n        meta[\"grid\"][(meta[\"nx\"], meta[\"ny\"])], forces=(0.0, 0.0, -1.0e5)\n    )\n    model.add_load_case(pre_load)\n    slave_load = LoadCase(\"slave_uz_load\")\n    slave_load.add_nodal_load(meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1], forces=(0.0, 0.0, -5.0e3))\n", "numLines": 100, "startLine": 501, "requestedOffset": 501, "requestedLimit": 100, "totalLines": null, "wasTruncated": true}, "outputText": "", "durationMs": 0.0, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Read", "message": "100 lines from C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\tests\\test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": "(truncated)"}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
{"id": "reasoning-98a997a3-6b4e-5bdc-b187-b4cf98d10919-0", "sessionId": "d77c8371-229c-7034-6088-eaefcc4b4445", "turnId": "turn-6f19a1036e2fefd5642f253cb635b74b", "createdAt": 1792347185502, "updatedAt": 1792347185502, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "I need to add the external-derivative standalone check to `test_r4_follower_complete_reduced_derivative_matches_finite_differences`. Per the supervisor:\n\n\"check the external reduced-force derivative on its own scale. With pressure200Pa and steel stiffness, a relative full-K tolerance can hide an absent external load tangent. Differentiate J(u)^T F_ext(u) and compare to J.T K_ext J + geometric_tangent(u,F_ext), normalizing by that external matrix.\"\n\nSo: define `ext_reduced_force(q_vec) = mpc_map.reduce_force(u_q, -f_ext)` (external part only, i.e., derivative of J^T F_ext). FD it, compare with the external part of K_red. The external part of the reduced tangent: `mpc_map.reduce_tangent(u, 0*K_T, -f_ext, K_ext)` — i.e., reduce_tangent with zero internal force and K_T=0, f_int-f_ext = -f_ext, K_ext. That gives J.T K_ext J + geometric_tangent(u, F_ext) (the geometric term from the external force).\n\nLet me check the reduce_tangent signature: `map.reduce_tangent(u, K_T, F_int, K_ext)` — from the summary: \"reduce_tangent(u,K_T,F_int)\". With K_ext as 4th arg. The geometric term is computed from F_int (the net force passed). In the complete check they pass `f_int - f_ext` and K_ext. So for the external-only derivative: pass K_T=zero matrix (same sparsity), F = -f_ext, K_ext. That yields J^T K_ext J + geometric(-f_ext) = derivative of J^T F_ext... let me think: d/dq [J^T F_ext(u(q))] = J^T K_ext J + (geometric terms). The reduce_tangent presumably computes T^T (K + G(F))^T T-ish... Actually the exact form: reduce_tangent(u, K_T, F, K_ext) = J^T K_T J + J^T K_ext J + H(F) where H is the MPC geometric Hessian from force F. For the external-only: derivative of J^T F_ex